<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ALH> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "alh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "alh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Alawa"@alh; skos:definition "Alawa is a moribund Australian Aboriginal language spoken by the Alawa people of the Northern Territory. By 2021, the number of people speaking it at home had dropped to 5. Alawa is a member of the Arnhem, or Macro-Gunwinyguan family, the second-largest Australian language family after Pama–Nyungan, but this language family is not universally accepted."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Alawa"@en .
