<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/CEY> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "cey"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "cey"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Ekai"@cey, "Lawktu"@en, "Läoktü"@en; skos:definition "Ekai Chin, also known as Läoktü Chin, is a Tibeto-Burman language falling under the Kuki-Chin sub-branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family. The Ekai are the largest group along Dalet Stream in northern Ann Township, Rakhine State, Myanmar. Compared to Sinitic languages, Kuki-Chin languages are tonal but less so, and they are less isolating and more morphologically structured. They also tend to display areal features with neighbouring Austro-Asiatic languages."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Ekai Chin"@en .
