<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/EMI> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "emi"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "emi"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Mussau-Emira"@emi; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "mussau-Emira"@emi .
<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/EMK> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "emk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "emk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "malinke"@emk, "maninkakan"@emk, "keleti maninka"@hu; skos:definition "Maninka (also known as Malinke), or more precisely Eastern Maninkakan, is the name of several closely related languages and dialects of the southeastern Manding subgroup of the Mande language family. It is the mother tongue of the Malinké people in Guinea, where it is spoken by 3.1 million people and is the main language in the Upper Guinea region, and in Mali, where the closely related Bambara is a national language, as well as in Liberia, Senegal, Sierra Leone and Ivory Coast, where it has no official status. It was the language of court and government during the Mali Empire. Mande languages are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "източен манинкакан"@bg, "východní maninkakan"@cs, "østmalinke"@da, "Ost-Maninkakan"@de, "Ανατολικά Μανινκανάν"@el, "Eastern Maninkakan"@en, "Maninkakan oriental"@es, "idamalinke"@et, "itämaninka"@fi, "maninkakan de l’Est"@fr, "Manancacáinis Oirthearach"@ga, "istočna maninka"@hr, "keleti malinké"@hu, "Maninkakan orientale"@it, "rytų maninkų"@lt, "austrumu maninkakanu"@lv, "Maninkakan tal-Lvant"@mt, "Oostelijk Maninkakan"@nl, "wschodni maninka"@pl, "maninca oriental"@pt, "maninka estică"@ro, "východný maninkakan"@sk, "vzhodna maninščina"@sl, "östmalinke"@sv .
