<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/IKH> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "ikh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "ikh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Arokho"@en, "Ikhin"@en, "Ikhin"@ikh; skos:definition "Ikhin-Arokho is an Edoid language spoken in Edo State in Nigeria. Together with Emai-Iuleha-Ora, it forms the Emaic subgroup. Similar to the more well-known Bantu languages, Ikhin-Arokho also features noun class systems, which are a key characteristic used to identify the broader Atlantic–Congo language family, to which Ikhin-Arokho belongs as part of the Volta–Congo primary branch."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Ikhin-Arokho"@en .
