<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/JAD> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "jad"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "jad"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "jahanka"@jad; skos:definition "Jahanka is a Manding language of Guinea-Bissau and Guinea. It is partially intelligible with Mandinka. Manding languages are a sub-branch of Mande languages that are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "джаханка"@bg, "džahanka"@cs, "jahanka"@da, "Jahanka"@de, "Τζαχάνκα"@el, "Jahanka"@en, "Jahanka"@es, "jahanka"@fi, "diakhanké"@fr, "Iahancais"@ga, "jahanke"@hr, "jahanka"@hu, "Jahanka"@it, "džahanka"@lt, "jahanku"@lv, "Jahanka"@mt, "Jahanka"@nl, "dżahanka"@pl, "jacanca"@pt, "jahanka"@ro, "jahanka"@sk, "džahanščina"@sl, "jahanka"@sv .
