<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/KAO> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "kao"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "kao"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kassonke"@en, "kasonke"@hr, "xaasongaxango"@kao; skos:definition "The Kassonke (Khassonké) language, Xaasongaxango (Xasonga) is a Manding language spoken by the Khassonké and Malinke of western Mali. Kassonke is an official language in Mali. Western and Eastern Maninka are 90% mutually intelligible, though distinct from the Mandinka (Malinke) of southern Senegal, which is a national language there. Manding languages are a sub-branch of Mande languages that are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "касонке"@bg, "xaasongaxango"@cs, "xaasongaxango"@da, "Xaasongaxango"@de, "Χασονγκαχάνγκο"@el, "Xaasongaxango"@en, "Xaasongaxango"@es, "hasonga"@et, "khasonka"@fi, "khassonké"@fr, "Sáisiongasaingis"@ga, "xaasongaxango"@hr, "kaszonga"@hu, "Xaasongaxango"@it, "hasonkų"@lt, "gāsongasengo"@lv, "Xaasongaxango"@mt, "Xaasongaxango"@nl, "kassonke"@pl, "cassonga"@pt, "xaasongaxango"@ro, "xaasongaxango"@sk, "hasonščina"@sl, "kassonke"@sv .
