<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/KMR> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "kmr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "kmr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kurmanji"@en, "Kurmancî"@kmr, "کورمانجی"@kmr; skos:definition "Northern Kurdish (Kurmanji) is a group of Kurdish dialects predominantly spoken in southeast Turkey, northwest Iran, northern Iraq and northern Syria. Northern Kurdish uses the Latin script. It is part of the Kurdish group within the northwestern branch of the Indo-Iranian languages."@en, "Le kurde septentrional (kurmanji) est un groupe de dialectes kurdes principalement parlés dans le Sud-Est de la Turquie, le Nord-Ouest de l’Iran, le Nord de l’Iraq et le Nord de la Syrie. Le kurde septentrional utilise l’alphabet latin. Il fait partie du groupe kurde de la branche nord-occidentale des langues indo-iraniennes."@fr; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "севернокюрдски"@bg, "severní kurdština"@cs, "nordkurdisk"@da, "Kurmandschi"@de, "βόρεια κουρδική"@el, "Northern Kurdish"@en, "kurdo septentrional"@es, "põhja-kurdi keel"@et, "Kurmandži"@fi, "kurde septentrional"@fr, "Curmainsis"@ga, "sjevernokurdski"@hr, "kurmanci"@hu, "kurmancî"@it, "šiaurės kurdų"@lt, "kurmandži"@lv, "Kurd tat-Tramuntana"@mt, "Noord-Koerdisch"@nl, "kurmanci"@pl, "curdo setentrional"@pt, "kurdă de nord"@ro, "severná kurdčina"@sk, "severna kurdščina"@sl, "nordkurdiska"@sv, "північнокурдська мова"@uk .
