<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/KUI> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "kui"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "kui"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kalapalo"@en, "Kalapálo"@kui, "Kuikúro"@kui; skos:definition "Kuikúro-Kalapálo is a Cariban language spoken by the Kuikuro and Kalapalo peoples in seven villages along the Culuene River in Brazil. Kuikúro-Kalapálo speak the same language but are ethnically distinct. A related Matipuhy language is spoken by the Matipu. Together, Kuikúro, Kalapálo and Matipuhy form the Nuclear Kuikuroan branch."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Kuikúro-Kalapálo"@en .
