<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/LSN> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "lsn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "lsn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "藏语手语"@lsn; skos:definition "Tibetan Sign Language is the recently established deaf sign language of Tibet. It is the first recognized sign language for a minority in China. The Tibetan Sign Language Project was set up under the supervision of Handicap International in 2001 to create a standardized language, based primarily on the existing sign language of Lhasa, as a replacement for the regional sign languages of Tibet."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Tibetan Sign Language"@en .
