<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/MLQ> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "mlq"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "mlq"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "nyugati maninka"@hu, "malinke"@mlq, "maninkakan"@mlq; skos:definition "Western Maninkakan (Maninka, Malinke) is a Manding language spoken by the Malinke of eastern Senegal. Western and Eastern Maninka are 90% mutually intelligible, though distinct from the Mandinka of southern Senegal, which is a national language there. Manding languages are a sub-branch of Mande languages that are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "западен манинкакан"@bg, "západní maninkakan"@cs, "vestmalinke"@da, "West-Maninkakan"@de, "Δυτικά Μανινκανάν"@el, "Western Maninkakan"@en, "Maninkakan occidental"@es, "läänemalinke"@et, "länsimaninka"@fi, "maninkakan de l’Ouest"@fr, "Manancacáinis Iartharach"@ga, "zapadna maninka"@hr, "nyugati malinké"@hu, "Maninkakan occidentale"@it, "vakarų maninkų"@lt, "rietumu maninkakanu"@lv, "Maninkakan tal-Punent"@mt, "Westelijk Maninkakan"@nl, "zachodni maninka"@pl, "maninca ocidental"@pt, "maninka vestică"@ro, "západný maninkakan"@sk, "zahodna maninščina"@sl, "västmalinke"@sv .
