<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/MVW> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "mvw"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "mvw"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Machinga"@mvw; skos:definition "Machinga is a Bantu language spoken in Tanzania and northern Mozambique. Together with Makonde (kde), Matambwe (wtb) and Ndonde Hamba (njd), it forms the Makonde group, which is classified within the Volta-Congo primary branch. Like other Bantu languages, Machinga has a noun class system, a characteristic feature of languages belonging to the Atlantic–Congo lineage, the largest demonstrated language family in Africa."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Machinga"@en .
