<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/MWK> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "mwk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "mwk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kita Maninka"@en, "središnja maninka"@hr, "középmaninka"@hu, "maninka-kita"@mwk; skos:definition "Kita Maninkakan, or Central Malinke, is a Manding language spoken by about a million people in Mali, where it is a national language. About 10% are ethnically Fula. Manding languages are a sub-branch of Mande languages that are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "кита-манинкакан"@bg, "kita maninkakan"@cs, "centralmalinke"@da, "Kita-Maninkakan"@de, "Κίτα Μανινκακάν"@el, "Kita Maninkakan"@en, "Kita maninkakan"@es, "Kita malinke"@et, "kitanmaninka"@fi, "kita maninkakan"@fr, "Manancacáinis Chíte"@ga, "kita maninka"@hr, "középmalinké"@hu, "Kita maninkakan"@it, "Kitos maninkų"@lt, "kita maninkakanu"@lv, "Kita Maninkakan"@mt, "Kita-Maninkakan"@nl, "kita maninka"@pl, "maninca de Kita"@pt, "maninka kita"@ro, "kita maninkakan"@sk, "malinščina"@sl, "centralmalinke"@sv .
