<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/NLO> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "nlo"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "nlo"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Ngul"@nlo; skos:definition "Ngul (also Ngwii) is a Bantu language spoken in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. Together with Lwel, Ding and Nzadi, it belongs to the West-Coastal Bantu group, which is classified within the Volta-Congo primary branch. Like other Bantu languages, Ngul has a noun class system, a characteristic feature of languages belonging to the Atlantic–Congo lineage, the largest demonstrated language family in Africa."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Ngul"@en .
