<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/RWL> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "rwl"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "rwl"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Luwira"@en, "Rwira"@en, "Kiruwila"@rwl; skos:definition "Ruwila, also spelled as Luwira, is a narrow Bantu language spoken in central Tanzania. Together with other Sukuma-Nyamwezi languages it is classified within the Volta-Congo primary branch. Like other Bantu languages, Ruwila has a noun class system, a characteristic feature of languages belonging to the Atlantic–Congo lineage, the largest demonstrated language family in Africa."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Ruwila"@en .
