<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/TAR> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "tar"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "tar"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Rarámuri (TAR)"@tar; skos:definition "Central Tarahumara is a Southern Uto-Aztecan language spoken in northern Mexico. Together with Lowland Tarahumara (tac), Southeastern Tarahumara (tcu), Northern Tarahumara (thh) and Southwestern Tarahumara (twr), it forms the Tarahumaran group. The native name of Tarahumara language is Rarámuri or Ralámuli ra'ícha."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Central Tarahumara"@en .
