<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/TRV> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "trv"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "trv"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Seediq"@en, "Taroko"@en, "Sediq"@trv; skos:definition "Sediq, also known as Seediq or Taroko, is an Atayalic language spoken in the mountains of northern Taiwan by the Sediq Toda, Seediq Tgdaya, and Seediq Truku people. Atayalic is one of the primary branches of the Austronesian language family."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Sediq"@en .
