<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/TRX> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "trx"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "trx"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Mbaan"@trx, "Tringgus"@trx; skos:definition "Tringgus-Sembaan Bidayuh is a Dayak language of Borneo. It is closely related to the Bukar-Sadung Bidayuh (sdo), Bau Bidayuh (sne) and Biatah Bidayuh (bth) languages. Tringgus-Sembaan Bidayuh belongs to the Malayo-Polyneasian primary branch of the Austronesian language family. Two main morphological characteristics of the Malayo-Polynesian languages are a system of affixation and reduplication to form new words."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Tringgus-Sembaan Bidayuh"@en .
