<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/USS> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "uss"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "uss"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Western Duka"@en, "Saare"@uss; skos:definition "us-Saare, also known as Western Duka, is a Northwestern Kainji language of Nigeria. It is close to ut-Hun, also known as Eastern Duka. However, speakers use Saare for both languages. Noun class systems are a defining feature of the Atlantic–Congo languages, to which Kainji languages belong as part of the Volta-Congo primary branch and the Benue-Congo sub-branch."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "us-Saare"@en .
