<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/UWA> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "uwa"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "uwa"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kuku-Uwanh"@uwa; skos:definition "Kuku-Uwanh is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language spoken by Wik peoples on the Cape York Peninsula of Queensland. Kuku-Uwanh is closely related to Kuku-Muminh (xmh) and to Kuku-Mu'inh (xmp). All belong to the Paman sub-branch within the Pama–Nyungan language family, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Kuku-Uwanh"@en .
