<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WKR> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "wkr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "wkr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kurnkopanut"@wkr; skos:definition "Keerray-Woorroong, also known as Kurnkopanut, is a Pama-Nyungan language spoken in Western District of Victoria, Australia. Together with its close relatives, it forms the Warrnambool dialect continuum and with slightly more distant Bunganditj the Warrnambool-Bunganditj group. The Pama–Nyungan languages are the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Keerray-Woorroong"@en .
