<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WLY> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "wly"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "wly"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Waling"@wly; skos:definition "Waling is a dormant Kiranti language previously spoken in the eastern Himalayan hills of eastern Nepal by Kirati Bantawa ethnic groups. It is closely related to Bantawa (bap). The Kiranti languages form a branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family, one of the largest language families in the world. Kirati Bantawa groups use a syllabic alphabet system known as Kirat Rai."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Waling"@en .
