<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WWR> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "wwr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "wwr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Warrwa"@wwr; skos:definition "Warrwa is an extinct Australian Aboriginal language formerly spoken in the Derby Region of Western Australia, near Broome. It is closely related to the Nyikina language (nyh). Both belong to the small Nyulnyulan language family. Most languages in this family are extinct, with only three extant languages, all of which are almost extinct."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Warrwa"@en .
