<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WYN> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "wyn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "wyn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Wyandotte"@en, "Wandat"@wyn; skos:definition "Wyandot (also Wyandotte, Wandat) is the Iroquoian language traditionally spoken by the people known as Wyandot or Wyandotte, descended from the Tionontati. It is considered a sister to the Huron-Wendat language, spoken by descendants of the Huron-Wendat Confederacy."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Wyandot"@en .
