<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/XKK> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "xkk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "xkk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kaco'"@en, "Kachok'"@xkk; skos:definition "Kachok (Kacoʼ) belongs to the Bahnaric primary branch of the Austroasiatic language family. It is spoken in northeastern Cambodia, especially in Ratanakiri Province. Together with its closest relative, Romam, Kachok forms the Lamamic group, though the two languages are quite distinct."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Kachok'"@en .
