<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ZZA> ccmm_props:ISO_639_2B "zza"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2B>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2T "zza"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2T>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "zza"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "zza"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Zazakî"@zza, "زازاکی"@zza; skos:definition "Zaza is an Indo-Iranian language spoken primarily in eastern Turkey by the Zazas, who are commonly considered as Kurds, and in many cases identify as such. The language is a part of the Zaza–Gorani language group of the northwestern group of the Iranian branch."@en; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "заза"@bg, "zázá"@cs, "zaza"@da, "Zazaisch"@de, "Ζαζάκι"@el, "Zaza"@en, "Zaza"@es, "zaza"@et, "zaza"@fi, "zaza"@fr, "Zazaicis"@ga, "zaza"@hr, "zazaki"@hu, "Zaza"@it, "zazų"@lt, "zaza"@lv, "Zaza"@mt, "Zazaki"@nl, "zazaki"@pl, "zaza"@pt, "zaza"@ro, "zazaština"@sk, "zazaščina"@sl, "zaza"@sv .
<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ZZJ> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "zzj"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "zzj"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "左江壮語"@zzj; skos:inScheme <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language>; skos:prefLabel "Zuojiang Zhuang"@en .
<http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_14cb> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "acceso a metadatos"@es, "acceso a metadatos solamente"@es, "acceso a registro bibliografico"@es, "acceso a registro bibliográfico"@es, "registro bibliografico"@es, "accès limité aux métadonnées"@fr, "accès restreint aux métadonnées"@fr, "accès uniquement aux métadonnées"@fr, "libre accès aux seules métadonnées"@fr, "alleen metadata beschikbaar"@nl, "acesso limitado a metadados"@pt, "samo dostop do metapodatkov"@sl, "sadece metadata erişimi"@tr; skos:definition "Přístup pouze k metadatům označuje zdroj, u něhož je přístup omezen pouze na metadata. Samotný zdroj je popsán metadaty, není však přímo dostupný prostřednictvím systému nebo platformy ani na něj nelze odkazovat prostřednictvím otevřeně přístupné kopie v externím časopise nebo důvěryhodném archivu."@cs, "Metadata only access refers to a resource in which access is limited to metadata only. The resource itself is described by the metadata, but neither is directly available through the system or platform nor can be referenced to an open access copy in an external journal or trustworthy archive."@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول المحدود بالميتاداتا"@ar, "accés només a metadades"@ca, "pouze metadata"@cs, "nur Metadaten"@de, "metadata only access"@en, "registro bibliográfico"@es, "vain metadata saatavissa"@fi, "accès aux seules métadonnées"@fr, "accesso limitato ai metadati"@it, "メタデータのみ"@ja, "toegang beperkt tot metadata"@nl, "acesso a metadados"@pt, "доступ к метаданным"@ru, "samo metapodatki"@sl, "pristup ograničen na metapodatke"@sr, "приступ ограничен на метаподатке"@sr-cyrl, "sadece üstveri erişimi"@tr; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.org/eprint/accessRights/ClosedAccess>; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_16ec> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "acceso bajo condiciones"@es, "acceso bajo restricciones"@es, "acceso con limitaciones"@es, "acceso gratuito bajo restricciones"@es, "acceso gratuito mediado"@es, "rajoitettu pääsy"@fi, "accès aux abonnés"@fr, "accès limité"@fr, "accès restreint"@fr, "accès sous condition"@fr, "beperkte toegang"@nl, "pristup s lozinkom"@sr, "приступ с лозинком"@sr-cyrl, "kısıtlı erişim"@tr; skos:definition """Omezený přístup označuje zdroj, který je v systému dostupný, avšak s určitým omezením bránícím plnému otevřenému přístupu. Tento typ přístupu může nastat v řadě různých situací. Několik příkladů je uvedeno níže:

Uživatel se musí pro přístup ke zdroji přihlásit do systému

Uživatel musí pro přístup ke zdroji zaslat e-mail autorovi nebo správci systému

Přístup ke zdroji je omezen na konkrétní komunitu (např. pouze na univerzitní komunitu)"""@cs, """Restricted access refers to a resource that is available in a system but with some type of restriction for full open access. This type of access can occur in a number of different situations. Some examples are described below:
The user must log-in to the system in order to access the resource
The user must send an email to the author or system administrator to access the resource
Access to the resource is restricted to a specific community (e.g. limited to a university community)"""@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول المقيد"@ar, "accés restringit"@ca, "omezený přístup"@cs, "eingeschränkter Zugang"@de, "restricted access"@en, "acceso restringido"@es, "rajoitettu saatavuus"@fi, "accès réservé"@fr, "accesso riservato"@it, "アクセス制限有"@ja, "beperkt toegankelijk"@nl, "acesso restrito"@pt, "ограниченный доступ"@ru, "omejen dostop"@sl, "ograničeni pristup"@sr, "ограничени приступ"@sr-cyrl, "sınırlı erişim"@tr; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.org/eprint/accessRights/RestrictedAccess>, <https://vocabs.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/archeaccessrestrictions/restricted>; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_abf2> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "freier Zugang"@de, "acceso abierto gratuito"@es, "acceso público"@es, "vapaa pääsy"@fi, "accès libre"@fr, "accès ouvert"@fr, "open access"@fr, "vrij beschikbaar"@nl, "acesso livre"@pt, "бесплатный доступ"@ru; skos:definition "Otevřený přístup označuje zdroj, který je okamžitě a trvale dostupný online a volně přístupný všem na webu, bez finančních a technických překážek. Zdroj je buď uložen v repozitáři, nebo je na něj odkazováno v externím časopise či důvěryhodném archivu."@cs, "Open access refers to a resource that is immediately and permanently online, and free for all on the Web, without financial and technical barriers.The resource is either stored in the repository or referenced to an external journal or trustworthy archive."@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول الحر"@ar, "accés obert"@ca, "otevřený přístup"@cs, "offener Zugang"@de, "open access"@en, "acceso abierto"@es, "avoin saatavuus"@fi, "libre accès"@fr, "accesso aperto"@it, "オープンアクセス"@ja, "vrij toegankelijk"@nl, "acesso aberto"@pt, "открытый доступ"@ru, "odprti dostop"@sl, "otvoreni pristup"@sr, "отворени приступ"@sr-cyrl, "açık erişim"@tr; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.org/eprint/accessRights/OpenAccess>, <https://vocabs.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/archeaccessrestrictions/public>; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_f1cf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "acceso bajo periodo de embargo"@es, "acceso bajo período de embargo"@es, "acceso con periodo de carencia"@es, "acceso con periodo de embargo"@es, "deposito oscuro"@es, "depósito oscuro"@es, "accès libre retardé"@fr, "accès sous embargo"@fr, "libre accès après durée d'embargo"@fr, "libre accès différé"@fr, "acesso sob embargo"@pt, "dostop z embargom"@sl; skos:definition "Odložené zpřístupnění označuje zdroj, který je do určitého data dostupný pouze v režimu přístupu k metadatům a teprve poté je uvolněn do otevřeného přístupu. Embargo může být vyžadováno politikami vydavatelů a poskytovatelů financování nebo stanoveno autorem (např. v případě závěrečných prací a disertací)."@cs, "Embargoed access refers to a resource that is metadata only access until released for open access on a certain date. Embargoes can be required by publishers and funders policies, or set by the author (e.g such as in the case of theses and dissertations)."@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول المحظور"@ar, "accés embargat"@ca, "odložené zpřístupnění"@cs, "Zugang unterliegt Embargo"@de, "embargoed access"@en, "acceso embargado"@es, "embargo"@fi, "sous embargo"@fr, "accesso sottoposto a periodo di embargo"@it, "エンバーゴ有"@ja, "onder embargo"@nl, "acesso embargado"@pt, "доступ с эмбарго"@ru, "odlog javne objave"@sl, "odloženi otvoreni pristup"@sr, "одложени отворени приступ"@sr-cyrl, "ambargolu erişim"@tr; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> dcterms:contributor "COAR Controlled Vocabularies Interest Group"; dcterms:creator "Alberto Apollaro", "Brigit Nonó", "Cristina Azorín", "Dan Liu", "Dom Fripp", "Gültekin Gürdal", "Hilary Jones", "Ilkay Holt", "Iryna Solodovnik", "Isabel Bernal", "Jochen Schirrwagen", "Juha Hakala", "Ku (Alan) Liping", "Laurence Le Borgne", "Marina Losada", "Milan Ojsteršek", "Milica Sevkusic", "Nathalie Vedovotto", "Nie Hua", "Paola Azrilevich", "Pavel Kotlík", "Pedro Príncipe", "Sawsan Habre", "Sophie Aubin", "Susanna Mornati", "Tomoko Kataoka", "Tomoya Shiota", "Wilko Steinhoff", "Yutaka Hayashi"; dcterms:description "The Access Rights vocabulary defines concepts to declare the access status of a resource. Multilingual labels regard regional distinctions in language and term."; dcterms:modified "2026-03-11T08:26:19+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime; dcterms:title "Access Rights"; a skos:ConceptScheme; rdfs:label "Access Rights"; skos:hasTopConcept <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_14cb>, <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_16ec>, <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_abf2>, <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_f1cf> .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/1YTN-RJZE> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "documents judicials"@ca, "retsprotokoller"@da, "Gerichtsakte"@de, "Gerichtsdokumente"@de, "document des tribunaux"@fr, "documentation judiciaire"@fr, "matériel juridique"@fr, "documenti giudiziari"@it, "documentos judiciais"@pt, "acte judiciare"@ro, "dokumenti sodišč"@sl, "sodni spisi"@sl; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D016418>, <https://sparontologies.github.io/fabio/current/fabio.html#d4e3790>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/RMP5-3GQ6>; skos:definition "A set of judicial proceedings that record, physically or digitally, and in an orderly fashion, the development of a process or procedural actions so that they may be recorded and examined by the parties. This would include the set of judicial proceedings and any item within that set as a physical or electronic court document. Adapted from https://dpej.rae.es/lema/expediente-judicial with input from https://www.supremecourt.gov/case_documents.aspx"@en; skos:editorialNote "New concept included for version 4 or resource types Vocab"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "وثائق قضائية"@ar, "hüquqi sənədlər"@az, "expedient judicial"@ca, "retsdokumenter"@da, "Prozessakte"@de, "δικαστικά έγγραφα"@el, "court documents"@en, "expediente judicial"@es, "oikeudenkäyntiasiakirjat"@fi, "document judiciaire"@fr, "expediente xudicial"@gl, "bírósági dokumentumok"@hu, "atti giudiziari"@it, "裁判所文書"@ja, "법원문서"@ko, "gerechtelijke documenten"@nl, "processos judiciais"@pt, "documente judiciare"@ro, "sodni dokumenti"@sl, "rättsliga dokument"@sv, "adli belgeler"@tr, "судові матеріали"@uk, "法庭文件"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/2H0M-X761> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "dades geogràfiques"@ca, "locatie data"@nl, "prostorni podaci"@sr, "просторни подаци"@sr-cyrl, "jeo uzamsal veri"@tr; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/Dataset>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_ddb1>; skos:definition "Geospatial data are any type of data with spatial coordinates that allow them to be mapped to the Earth's surface. They can represent physical objects, discrete areas or continuous surfaces. Discrete geospatial data are usually represented using vector data consisting of points, lines and polygons, while continuous geospatial data are usually represented by raster data, consisting of a grid of cells that each has its own value. Any number of applications in a wide range of areas produce geospatial data, such as GIS, Remote Sensing equipment, GPS units, archaeological total stations, manual mapping and computer-aided design (CAD), in a number of formats, including images, vector, text, and tabular data. Vector-based geospatial data include tables listing archaeological sites along with their coordinates, text-based files (e.g., XML) containing coordinates and topology for historic road networks, voting figures for political parties by administrative area. Raster-based geospatial data include satellite images, aerial photographs, scanned maps, and digital maps of elevations, vegetation, land-use, sea surface temperatures, air pollution, soil-types, etc. [Source: https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/GeneralDataFormat_2.0.html]"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "بيانات جغرافية"@ar, "geoməkan məlumatları"@az, "dades geoespacials"@ca, "geospatiale data"@da, "Geodaten"@de, "γεωχωρικά δεδομένα"@el, "geospatial data"@en, "datos geoespaciales"@es, "paikkatieto"@fi, "donnée géospatiale"@fr, "datos xeoespaciais"@gl, "térinformációs adatok"@hu, "dati geospaziali"@it, "地理空間データ"@ja, "지리공간 데이터"@ko, "geospatiale gegevens"@nl, "dados geoespaciais"@pt, "date geospațiale"@ro, "геопространственные данные"@ru, "geoprostorski podatki"@sl, "geoprostorni podaci"@sr, "геопросторни подаци"@sr-cyrl, "geospatiala data"@sv, "coğrafi uzamsal veri"@tr, "геопросторові дані"@uk, "地理空间数据"@zh; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D005842>, <http://purl.dataone.org/odo/SALMON_00000675> .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/43KC-T6DC> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "articolo scientifico"@it, "članak u magazinu"@sr, "чланак у магазину"@sr-cyrl; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_2cd9>; skos:definition "An Item appearing in a magazine (a general interest or specific focus periodical). This item is often shorter in length, is submitted by in-house and external authors. Adapted from MAGAZINE Definition & Meaning - Black's Law Dictionary (thelawdictionary.org)"@en; skos:editorialNote "New concept added to be included in upcoming version 4.0"@en; skos:exactMatch <https://sparontologies.github.io/fabio/current/fabio.html#d4e3866>; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "مقال في مجلة"@ar, "jurnal məqaləsi"@az, "article de divulgació"@ca, "magasinartikel"@da, "Zeitschriftenartikel"@de, "άρθρο περιοδικού"@el, "magazine article"@en, "artículo de magacín"@es, "aikakauslehtiartikkeli"@fi, "article de magazine"@fr, "artigo de revista divulgativa"@gl, "magazincikk"@hu, "articolo in rivista"@it, "雑誌記事"@ja, "잡지 기사"@ko, "tijdschriftartikel"@nl, "artigo em revista"@pt, "časopisni članek"@sl, "članak u informativnoj reviji"@sr, "чланак у информативној ревији"@sr-cyrl, "artikel i magasin"@sv, "magazin makalesi"@tr, "стаття у журналі"@uk .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/542X-3S04> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "design"@ro, "dizajn"@sl; skos:definition "Plans, drawing or set of drawings showing how something e.g. building, product is to be made and how it will work and look. [Source: Adapted from https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/design]"@en; skos:exactMatch <https://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/ncimbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI%20Metathesaurus&code=C1707689>; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:narrower <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/BW7T-YM2G>, <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/JBNF-DYAD>; skos:prefLabel "تصميم"@ar, "dizayn"@az, "disseny"@ca, "formgivning"@da, "Entwurf"@de, "σχεδίαση"@el, "design"@en, "diseño"@es, "suunnitelma"@fi, "schéma"@fr, "deseño"@gl, "tervrajz"@hu, "design"@it, "デザイン"@ja, "디자인"@ko, "ontwerp"@nl, "desenho"@pt, "proiectare"@ro, "дизайн"@ru, "oblikovanje"@sl, "dizajn"@sr, "дизајн"@sr-cyrl, "design"@sv, "tasarım"@tr, "дизайн"@uk, "设计"@zh; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme> .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/63NG-B465> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "eksperimental məlumatlar"@az; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/Dataset>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_ddb1>; skos:definition "Data resulting from the experimental research method involving the manipulation of some or all of the independent variables included in the hypotheses. [Source: Adapted from https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "بيانات تجريبية"@ar, "sınaq məlumatları"@az, "dades experimentals"@ca, "eksperimentelle data"@da, "experimentelle Daten"@de, "πειραματικά δεδομένα"@el, "experimental data"@en, "datos experimentales"@es, "kokeellinen data"@fi, "donnée expérimentale"@fr, "datos experimentais"@gl, "kísérleti adatok"@hu, "dati sperimentali"@it, "実験データ"@ja, "실험 데이터"@ko, "experimentele data"@nl, "dados experimentais"@pt, "date experimentale"@ro, "экспериментальные данные"@ru, "eksperimentalni podatki"@sl, "eksperimentalni podaci"@sr, "експериментални подаци"@sr-cyrl, "experimentella data"@sv, "deneysel veri"@tr, "експериментальні дані"@uk, "实验数据"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/6NC7-GK9S> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "prepis"@sl, "誊写记录"@zh; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/Text>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_18cf>; skos:definition "A written record of words spoken in court proceedings or in a speech, interview, broadcast, or sound recording. [Source: Adapted from https://products.abc-clio.com/ODLIS/odlis_t.aspx]"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "نسخ نصي"@ar, "transkripsiya"@az, "transcripció"@ca, "transskription"@da, "Transkription"@de, "μεταγραφή"@el, "transcription"@en, "transcripción"@es, "litteroitu teksti"@fi, "transcription"@fr, "transcrición"@gl, "transzkripció"@hu, "trascrizione"@it, "文字起こし"@ja, "전사"@ko, "transcriptie"@nl, "transcrição"@pt, "transcriere"@ro, "транскрипция"@ru, "transkripcija"@sl, "transkript"@sr, "транскрипт"@sr-cyrl, "transkription"@sv, "transkripsiyon"@tr, "траскрипт"@uk, "转录资料"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/8KJG-QS0Y> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "equipament de laboratori"@ca, "instrumentació científica"@ca, "equipamiento de laboratorio"@es, "instrumentación científica"@es, "instrumentación científica"@gl, "strumento di ricerca"@it, "strumento scientifico"@it, "instrumento de pesquisa"@pt, "raziskovalni inštrument"@sl; skos:definition "A device, tool or apparatus used to obtain, measure and/or analyze data. Source https://datacite-metadata-schema.readthedocs.io/en/4.5/appendices/appendix-1/resourceTypeGeneral/#instrument"@en; skos:editorialNote "New concept included for version 4 of resource types Vocab"@en; skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/skgo/modsci#ScientificInstrument>; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "أداة بحث"@ar, "tədqiqat aləti"@az, "instrument de recerca"@ca, "forskningsinstrument"@da, "Forschungsinstrument"@de, "ερευνητικό εργαλείο"@el, "research instrument"@en, "instrumento de investigación"@es, "tutkimusväline"@fi, "instrument de recherche"@fr, "instrumento de investigación"@gl, "kutatási eszköz"@hu, "strumentazione"@it, "実験装置"@ja, "연구장비"@ko, "onderzoeksinstrument"@nl, "instrumento de investigação"@pt, "instrument de cercetare"@ro, "инструмент исследования"@ru, "raziskovalno orodje"@sl, "istraživački instrument"@sr, "истраживачки инструмент"@sr-cyrl, "forskningsinstrument"@sv, "araştırma cihazı"@tr, "інструмент дослідження"@uk, "研究工具"@zh; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme> .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/9DKX-KSAF> a skos:Concept; skos:broadMatch <https://sparontologies.github.io/fabio/current/fabio.html#d4e4175>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_15cd>; skos:definition "A special form of patent right granted by a state or jurisdiction to an inventor or the inventor’s assignee for a fixed period of time. The terms and conditions for granting a utility model are slightly different from those for normal patents (including a shorter term of protection and less stringent patentability requirements). The term can also describe what are known in certain countries as “petty patents,” “short-term patents” or “innovation patents.” [Source: https://www.wipo.int/edocs/pubdocs/en/wipo_pub_943_2018.pdf]"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "نموذج منفعة"@ar, "faydalı model"@az, "model d'utilitat"@ca, "brugsmodel"@da, "Gebrauchsmuster"@de, "μοντέλο χρησιμότητας"@el, "utility model"@en, "modelo de utilidad"@es, "hyödyllisyysmalli"@fi, "modèle d'utilité"@fr, "modelo de utilidade"@gl, "használati minta"@hu, "modello di utilità"@it, "実用新案"@ja, "실용신안"@ko, "gebruiksmodel"@nl, "modelo de utilidade"@pt, "model de utilitate"@ro, "полезная модель"@ru, "patent s skrajšanim trajanjem"@sl, "mali patent"@sr, "мали патент"@sr-cyrl, "bruksmodell"@sv, "faydalı model"@tr, "корисна модель"@uk, "实用新型专利"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/A8F1-NPV9> a skos:Concept; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/Dataset>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_ddb1>; skos:definition "Genomic data refers to the genome and DNA data of an organism. They are used in bioinformatics for collecting, storing and processing the genomes of living things. Genomic data is a more extensive term than sequencing data. However genomic data mostly come from sequencing techniques. It may include non-sequencing data such as data from microarrays, data from real-time PCR panels and data from pharmacogenomics studies. [Source: Adapted from https://www.techopedia.com/definition/31247/genomic-data]"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0004600>; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "بيانات جينومية"@ar, "genomik məlumatlar"@az, "dades genòmiques"@ca, "genomiske data"@da, "Genomdaten"@de, "γονιδιωματικά δεδομένα"@el, "genomic data"@en, "datos genómicos"@es, "genomidata"@fi, "donnée génomique"@fr, "datos xenómicos"@gl, "genomikai adatok"@hu, "dati genomici"@it, "ゲノムデータ"@ja, "지놈 데이터"@ko, "genomische data"@nl, "dados genómicos"@pt, "date genomice"@ro, "геномные данные"@ru, "genomski podatki"@sl, "genomski podaci"@sr, "геномски подаци"@sr-cyrl, "genomiska data"@sv, "genomik veri"@tr, "геномні дані"@uk, "基因组数据"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/ACF7-8YT9> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "بيانات تلخيصية"@ar, "toplanmış məlumatlar"@az, "date cumulate"@ro, "izpeljani podatki"@sl, "združeni podatki"@sl; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/Dataset>, <https://vocabs.lter-europe.net/elter_cl/en/page/10016>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_ddb1>; skos:definition "Statistics that relate to broad classes, groups, or categories. The data are averaged, totaled, or otherwise derived from individual-level data, and it is no longer possible to distinguish the characteristics of individuals within those classes, groups, or categories. For example, the number and age group of the unemployed in specific geographic regions, or national level statistics on the occurrence of specific offences, originally derived from the statistics of individual police districts. [Source: https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "بيانات مدمجة"@ar, "ümumiləşdirilmiş məlumatlar"@az, "dades agregades"@ca, "aggregerede data"@da, "aggregierte Daten"@de, "συγκεντρωτικά δεδομένα"@el, "aggregated data"@en, "datos agregados"@es, "aggregoitu tilastotieto"@fi, "données agrégées"@fr, "datos agregados"@gl, "aggregált adatok"@hu, "dati aggregati"@it, "集計データ"@ja, "집계 데이터"@ko, "geaggregeerde data"@nl, "dados agregados"@pt, "date agregate"@ro, "агрегированные данные"@ru, "agregirani podatki"@sl, "agregirani podaci"@sr, "агрегирани подаци"@sr-cyrl, "aggregerade data"@sv, "toplanmış veri"@tr, "агреговані дані"@uk, "聚合数据"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/AM6W-6QAW> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "donnée codée"@fr, "date codificate"@ro; skos:broadMatch <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/Dataset>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/c_ddb1>; skos:definition "Qualitative data (textual, video, audio or still-image) originally produced for other purposes into quantitative data (expressed in unit-by-variable matrices) by using coding techniques in accordance with pre-defined categorization schemes. For example, coded party manifesto data like the \"European Parliament Election Study 2009, Manifesto Study\" (doi:10.4232/1.10204)\". [Source: Adapted from https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en; skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/scheme>; skos:prefLabel "بيانات مشفرة"@ar, "kodlaşdırılmış məlumatlar"@az, "dades codificades"@ca, "kodede data"@da, "kodierte Daten"@de, "κωδικοποιημένα δεδομένα"@el, "encoded data"@en, "datos codificados"@es, "koodattu data"@fi, "donnée encodée"@fr, "datos codificados"@gl, "kódolt adatok"@hu, "dati codificati"@it, "符号化データ"@ja, "부호화 데이터"@ko, "geëncodeerde data"@nl, "dados codificados"@pt, "date criptate"@ro, "кодированные данные"@ru, "kodirani podatki"@sl, "kodirani podaci"@sr, "кодирани подаци"@sr-cyrl, "kodad data"@sv, "kodlanmış veri"@tr, "кодовані дані"@uk, "编码数据"@zh .
<http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/BW7T-YM2G> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "maquetació"@ca, "Layoutentwurf"@de, "kytkentäkaavio"@fi, "schéma d'implantation"@fr, "레이아웃 설계"@ko, "design de aspect"@ro, "design de machetă"@ro, "макетирование"@ru; skos:broadMatch <https://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/ncimbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI%20Metathesaurus&code=C1707689>; skos:broader <http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/542X-3S04>; skos:definition """Layout-design (topography) means the three-dimensional disposition, however expressed, of 
