pping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration; sssom:object_label "Date Copyrighted"; sssom:subject_label "Copyrighted" ], [ dcterms:created "2026-07-20"^^xsd:date; dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0852-6632>; owl:annotatedProperty skos:exactMatch; owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/dateType/Created>; owl:annotatedTarget <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Created>; a owl:Axiom; sssom:confidence 1e+00; sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration; sssom:object_label "Date Created"; sssom:subject_label "Created" ], [ dcterms:created "2026-07-20"^^xsd:date; dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0852-6632>; owl:annotatedProperty skos:exactMatch; owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/dateType/Issued>; owl:annotatedTarget <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Issued>; a owl:Axiom; sssom:confidence 1e+00; sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration; sssom:object_label "Date Issued"; sssom:subject_label "Issued" ], [ dcterms:created "2026-07-20"^^xsd:date; dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0852-6632>; owl:annotatedProperty skos:exactMatch; owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/dateType/Submitted>; owl:annotatedTarget <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Submitted>; a owl:Axiom; sssom:confidence 1e+00; sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration; sssom:object_label "Date Submitted"; sssom:subject_label "Submitted" ], [ dcterms:created "2026-07-20"^^xsd:date; dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0852-6632>; owl:annotatedProperty skos:exactMatch; owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/dateType/Updated>; owl:annotatedTarget <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Updated>; a owl:Axiom; sssom:confidence 1e+00; sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration; sssom:object_label "Date Updated"; sssom:subject_label "Updated" ], [ dcterms:created "2026-07-20"^^xsd:date; dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0852-6632>; owl:annotatedProperty skos:exactMatch; owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.org/datacite/v4.4/dateType/Valid>; owl:annotatedTarget <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Valid>; a owl:Axiom; sssom:confidence 1e+00; sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration; sssom:object_label "Date Valid"; sssom:subject_label "Valid" ] .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights/c_14cb> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "acceso a metadatos"@es, "acceso a metadatos solamente"@es, "acceso a registro bibliografico"@es, "acceso a registro bibliográfico"@es, "registro bibliografico"@es, "accès limité aux métadonnées"@fr, "accès restreint aux métadonnées"@fr, "accès uniquement aux métadonnées"@fr, "libre accès aux seules métadonnées"@fr, "alleen metadata beschikbaar"@nl, "acesso limitado a metadados"@pt, "samo dostop do metapodatkov"@sl, "sadece metadata erişimi"@tr; skos:definition "Přístup pouze k metadatům označuje zdroj, u něhož je přístup omezen pouze na metadata. Samotný zdroj je popsán metadaty, není však přímo dostupný prostřednictvím systému nebo platformy ani na něj nelze odkazovat prostřednictvím otevřeně přístupné kopie v externím časopise nebo důvěryhodném archivu."@cs, "Metadata only access refers to a resource in which access is limited to metadata only. The resource itself is described by the metadata, but neither is directly available through the system or platform nor can be referenced to an open access copy in an external journal or trustworthy archive."@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_14cb>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول المحدود بالميتاداتا"@ar, "accés només a metadades"@ca, "pouze metadata"@cs, "nur Metadaten"@de, "metadata only access"@en, "registro bibliográfico"@es, "vain metadata saatavissa"@fi, "accès aux seules métadonnées"@fr, "accesso limitato ai metadati"@it, "メタデータのみ"@ja, "toegang beperkt tot metadata"@nl, "acesso a metadados"@pt, "доступ к метаданным"@ru, "samo metapodatki"@sl, "pristup ograničen na metapodatke"@sr, "приступ ограничен на метаподатке"@sr-cyrl, "sadece üstveri erişimi"@tr; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.org/eprint/accessRights/ClosedAccess>; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights/c_16ec> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "acceso bajo condiciones"@es, "acceso bajo restricciones"@es, "acceso con limitaciones"@es, "acceso gratuito bajo restricciones"@es, "acceso gratuito mediado"@es, "rajoitettu pääsy"@fi, "accès aux abonnés"@fr, "accès limité"@fr, "accès restreint"@fr, "accès sous condition"@fr, "beperkte toegang"@nl, "pristup s lozinkom"@sr, "приступ с лозинком"@sr-cyrl, "kısıtlı erişim"@tr; skos:definition """Omezený přístup označuje zdroj, který je v systému dostupný, avšak s určitým omezením bránícím plnému otevřenému přístupu. Tento typ přístupu může nastat v řadě různých situací. Několik příkladů je uvedeno níže:

Uživatel se musí pro přístup ke zdroji přihlásit do systému

Uživatel musí pro přístup ke zdroji zaslat e-mail autorovi nebo správci systému

Přístup ke zdroji je omezen na konkrétní komunitu (např. pouze na univerzitní komunitu)"""@cs, """Restricted access refers to a resource that is available in a system but with some type of restriction for full open access. This type of access can occur in a number of different situations. Some examples are described below:
The user must log-in to the system in order to access the resource
The user must send an email to the author or system administrator to access the resource
Access to the resource is restricted to a specific community (e.g. limited to a university community)"""@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_16ec>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول المقيد"@ar, "accés restringit"@ca, "omezený přístup"@cs, "eingeschränkter Zugang"@de, "restricted access"@en, "acceso restringido"@es, "rajoitettu saatavuus"@fi, "accès réservé"@fr, "accesso riservato"@it, "アクセス制限有"@ja, "beperkt toegankelijk"@nl, "acesso restrito"@pt, "ограниченный доступ"@ru, "omejen dostop"@sl, "ograničeni pristup"@sr, "ограничени приступ"@sr-cyrl, "sınırlı erişim"@tr; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.org/eprint/accessRights/RestrictedAccess>, <https://vocabs.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/archeaccessrestrictions/restricted>; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights/c_abf2> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "freier Zugang"@de, "acceso abierto gratuito"@es, "acceso público"@es, "vapaa pääsy"@fi, "accès libre"@fr, "accès ouvert"@fr, "open access"@fr, "vrij beschikbaar"@nl, "acesso livre"@pt, "бесплатный доступ"@ru; skos:definition "Otevřený přístup označuje zdroj, který je okamžitě a trvale dostupný online a volně přístupný všem na webu, bez finančních a technických překážek. Zdroj je buď uložen v repozitáři, nebo je na něj odkazováno v externím časopise či důvěryhodném archivu."@cs, "Open access refers to a resource that is immediately and permanently online, and free for all on the Web, without financial and technical barriers.The resource is either stored in the repository or referenced to an external journal or trustworthy archive."@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_abf2>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول الحر"@ar, "accés obert"@ca, "otevřený přístup"@cs, "offener Zugang"@de, "open access"@en, "acceso abierto"@es, "avoin saatavuus"@fi, "libre accès"@fr, "accesso aperto"@it, "オープンアクセス"@ja, "vrij toegankelijk"@nl, "acesso aberto"@pt, "открытый доступ"@ru, "odprti dostop"@sl, "otvoreni pristup"@sr, "отворени приступ"@sr-cyrl, "açık erişim"@tr; skos:relatedMatch <http://purl.org/eprint/accessRights/OpenAccess>, <https://vocabs.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/archeaccessrestrictions/public>; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights/c_f1cf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "acceso bajo periodo de embargo"@es, "acceso bajo período de embargo"@es, "acceso con periodo de carencia"@es, "acceso con periodo de embargo"@es, "deposito oscuro"@es, "depósito oscuro"@es, "accès libre retardé"@fr, "accès sous embargo"@fr, "libre accès après durée d'embargo"@fr, "libre accès différé"@fr, "acesso sob embargo"@pt, "dostop z embargom"@sl; skos:definition "Odložené zpřístupnění označuje zdroj, který je do určitého data dostupný pouze v režimu přístupu k metadatům a teprve poté je uvolněn do otevřeného přístupu. Embargo může být vyžadováno politikami vydavatelů a poskytovatelů financování nebo stanoveno autorem (např. v případě závěrečných prací a disertací)."@cs, "Embargoed access refers to a resource that is metadata only access until released for open access on a certain date. Embargoes can be required by publishers and funders policies, or set by the author (e.g such as in the case of theses and dissertations)."@en; skos:editorialNote "Published"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/c_f1cf>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/accessrights>; skos:prefLabel "الوصول المحظور"@ar, "accés embargat"@ca, "odložené zpřístupnění"@cs, "Zugang unterliegt Embargo"@de, "embargoed access"@en, "acceso embargado"@es, "embargo"@fi, "sous embargo"@fr, "accesso sottoposto a periodo di embargo"@it, "エンバーゴ有"@ja, "onder embargo"@nl, "acesso embargado"@pt, "доступ с эмбарго"@ru, "odlog javne objave"@sl, "odloženi otvoreni pristup"@sr, "одложени отворени приступ"@sr-cyrl, "ambargolu erişim"@tr; skos:topConceptOf <http://purl.org/coar/access_right/scheme> .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles> a skos:ConceptScheme .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/contactperson> dc:identifier "ContactPerson"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person with knowledge of how to access, troubleshoot, or otherwise field issues related to the resource.
May also be the “Point of Contact” in an organisation that controls access to the resource, if that organisation is different from the Publisher, Distributor, and Data Manager."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/ContactPerson>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Kontaktní osoba"@cs, "Contact Person"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/datacollector> dc:identifier "DataCollector"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person/institution responsible for finding or gathering/collecting data under the guidelines of the author(s) or Principal Investigator (PI).
May also be used when crediting survey conductors, interviewers, event or condition observers, or persons responsible for monitoring key instrument data."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/DataCollector>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Sběratel dat"@cs, "Data Collector"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/datacurator> dc:identifier "DataCurator"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person tasked with reviewing, enhancing, cleaning, or standardizing metadata and the associated data submitted for storage, use, and maintenance within a data centre or repository.
While the DataManager is concerned with digital maintenance, the DataCurator’s role encompasses quality assurance focused on content and metadata. DataCurator responsibilities include: checking completeness of the submitted dataset against the content as described by the submitter; verifying standard metadata according to the applicable system or schema; adding or verifying specialized metadata to add value and ensure access across disciplines; and determining how the metadata might map to search engines, database products, and automated feeds.

Repository managers as well as data librarians working in the repository fall within this category."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/DataCurator>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Kurátor dat"@cs, "Data Curator"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/datamanager> dc:identifier "DataManager"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person (or organisation with a staff of data managers, such as a data centre) responsible for maintaining the finished resource.
The work done by this person or organisation ensures that the resource is periodically “refreshed” in terms of software/hardware support, is kept available or is protected from unauthorized access, is stored in accordance with industry standards, and is handled in accordance with the records management requirements applicable to it."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/DataManager>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Manažer dat"@cs, "Data Manager"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/distributor> dc:identifier "Distributor"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Institution tasked with responsibility to generate/disseminate copies of the resource in either electronic or print form.
Works stored in more than one archive/repository may credit each as a distributor."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Distributor>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Distributor"@cs, "Distributor"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/editor> dc:identifier "Editor"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """A person who oversees the details related to the publication format of the resource.
Note: if the Editor is to be credited in place of multiple creators, the Editor’s name may be supplied as Creator, with “(Ed.)” appended to the name."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Editor>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Editor"@cs, "Editor"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/hostinginstitution> dc:identifier "HostingInstitution"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Typically, the organisation allowing the resource to be available on the internet through the provision of its hardware/software/operating support.
This role normally falls on the University, research center or organization where the data center/data repository belongs."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/HostingInstitution>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Hostující instituce"@cs, "Hosting Institution"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/other> dc:identifier "Other"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Any person or institution making a significant contribution to the development and/or maintenance of the resource, but whose contribution is not adequately described by any of the other values for contributorType.
Could be a photographer, artist, or writer whose contribution helped to publicize the resource (as opposed to creating it), a reviewer of the resource, someone providing administrative services to the author (such as depositing updates into an online repository, analysing usage, etc.), or one of many other roles."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Other>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Jiná role"@cs, "Other"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/producer> dc:identifier "Producer"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Typically, a person or organisation responsible for the artistry and form of a media product.
In the data industry, this may be a company “producing” DVDs that package data for future dissemination by a distributor."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Producer>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Producent"@cs, "Producer"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/projectleader> dc:identifier "ProjectLeader"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person officially designated as head of project team or sub- project team instrumental in the work necessary to development of the resource.
The Project Leader is not “removed” from the work that resulted in the resource; he or she remains intimately involved throughout the life of the particular project team."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/ProjectLeader>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Vedoucí projektu"@cs, "Project Leader"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/projectmanager> dc:identifier "ProjectManager"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person officially designated as manager of a project. Project may consist of one or many project teams and sub-teams.
The manager of a project normally has more administrative responsibility than actual work involvement."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/ProjectManager>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Projektový manažer"@cs, "Project Manager"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/projectmember> dc:identifier "ProjectMember"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person on the membership list of a designated project/project team.
This vocabulary may or may not indicate the quality, quantity, or substance of the person’s involvement."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/ProjectMember>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Člen projektového týmu"@cs, "Project Member"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/registrationagency> dc:identifier "RegistrationAgency"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Institution/organisation officially appointed by a Registration Authority to handle specific tasks within a defined area of responsibility.
DataCite is a Registration Agency for the International DOI Foundation (IDF). One of DataCite’s tasks is to assign DOI prefixes to the allocating agents who then assign the full, specific character string to data clients, provide metadata back to the DataCite registry, etc."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/RegistrationAgency>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Registrační agentura"@cs, "Registration Agency"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/registrationauthority> dc:identifier "RegistrationAuthority"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """A standards-setting body from which Registration Agencies obtain official recognition and guidance.
The IDF serves as the Registration Authority for the International Standards Organisation (ISO) in the area/domain of Digital Object Identifiers."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/RegistrationAuthority>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Registrační autorita"@cs, "Registration Authority"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/relatedperson> dc:identifier "RelatedPerson"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """A person without a specifically defined role in the development of the resource, but who is someone the author wishes to recognize.
Usage Notes: This person could be an author’s intellectual mentor, a person providing intellectual leadership in the discipline or subject domain, etc."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/RelatedPerson>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Související osoba"@cs, "Related Person"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/researcher> dc:identifier "Researcher"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """A person involved in analysing data or the results of an experiment or formal study. May indicate an intern or assistant to one of the authors who helped with research but who was not so “key” as to be listed as an author.
Should be a person, not an institution. Note that a person involved in the gathering of data would fall under the contributorType “DataCollector.” The researcher may find additional data online and correlate it to the data collected for the experiment or study, for example."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Researcher>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Výzkumník"@cs, "Researcher"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/researchgroup> dc:identifier "ResearchGroup"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Typically refers to a group of individuals with a lab, department, or division that has a specifically defined focus of activity.
May operate at a narrower level of scope; may or may not hold less administrative responsibility than a project team."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/ResearchGroup>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Výzkumná skupina"@cs, "Research Group"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/rightsholder> dc:identifier "RightsHolder"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Person or institution owning or managing property rights, including intellectual property rights over the resource."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/RightsHolder>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Majitel práv"@cs, "Rights Holder"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/sponsor> dc:identifier "Sponsor"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """Person or organisation that issued a contract or under the auspices of which a work has been written, printed, published, developed, etc.
Includes organisations that provide in-kind support, through donation, provision of people or a facility or instrumentation necessary for the development of the resource, etc."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Sponsor>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Sponzor"@cs, "Sponsor"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/supervisor> dc:identifier "Supervisor"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Designated administrator over one or more groups/teams working to produce a resource, or over one or more steps of a development process."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Supervisor>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Supervizor"@cs, "Supervisor"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/translator> dc:identifier "Translator"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """A person, organization, or automated system responsible for converting the content of a resource from one language into another, preserving its meaning and intended message.
This contributor type should be applied to DOI metadata for a resource which has been translated from another resource."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/Translator>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Překladatel"@cs, "Translator"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles/workpackageleader> dc:identifier "WorkPackageLeader"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "A Work Package is a recognized data product, not all of which is included in publication. The package, instead, may include notes, discarded documents, etc. The Work Package Leader is responsible for ensuring the comprehensive contents, versioning, and availability of the Work Package during the development of the resource."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/AgentRole/Contributor/WorkPackageLeader>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/contributorsroles>; skos:prefLabel "Vedoucí pracovního balíku"@cs, "Work Package Leader"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/accepted> dc:identifier "Accepted"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date that the publisher accepted the resource into their system.
To indicate the start of an embargo period, use Accepted or Submitted, as appropriate."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Accepted>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum přijetí datasetu"@cs, "Date Accepted"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/available> dc:identifier "Available"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date the resource is made publicly available. May be a range.
To indicate the end of an embargo period, use Available."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Available>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum zveřejnění datasetu"@cs, "Date Available"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/collected> dc:identifier "Collected"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date in which the resource content was collected.
To indicate precise or particular timeframes in which research was conducted."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Collected>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum sběru dat"@cs, "Date Collected"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/copyrighted> dc:identifier "Copyrighted"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "The specific, documented date at which the resource receives a copyrighted status, if applicable."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Copyrighted>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum udělení copyrightu"@cs, "Date Copyrighted"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/coverage> dc:identifier "Coverage"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date that the resource content applies to, describes, or covers.
 To indicate the temporal coverage of the resource, use Coverage. This may be different from Collected."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Coverage>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Časové pokrytí datasetu"@cs, "Date Coverage"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/created> dc:identifier "Created"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date the resource itself was put together; this could refer to a timeframe in ancient history, a single date for a final component, e.g., the finalised file with all the data.
Recommended for discovery."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Created>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum vytvoření datasetu"@cs, "Date Created"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/issued> dc:identifier "Issued"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "The date that the resource is published or distributed, e.g., to a data centre."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Issued>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum vydání datasetu"@cs, "Date Issued"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/other> dc:identifier "Other"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Other date that does not fit into an existing category."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Other>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Jiné datum"@cs, "Other date"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/submitted> dc:identifier "Submitted"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date the creator submits the resource to the publisher. This could be different from Accepted if the publisher then applies a selection process.
Recommended for discovery."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Submitted>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum podání datasetu"@cs, "Date Submitted"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/updated> dc:identifier "Updated"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "The date of the last update to the resource, when the resource is being added to."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Updated>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum aktualizace datasetu"@cs, "Date Updated"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/valid> dc:identifier "Valid"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "The date during which the dataset or resource is accurate."@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Valid>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum platnosti datasetu"@cs, "Date Valid"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes/withdrawn> dc:identifier "Withdrawn"; a skos:Concept; skos:definition """The date the resource is removed.
 It is good practice to include a description that indicates the reason for the retraction or withdrawal."""@en; skos:exactMatch <https://vocabs.ccmm.cz/registry/codelist/TimeReference/Withdrawn>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/datetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Datum odstranění datasetu"@cs, "Date Withdrawn"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/7z> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "7-Zip compressed file"@en; skos:definition "7z is a compressed archive file format that supports several different data compression, encryption and pre-processing algorithms."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/7Z>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "7z"@en, "7z"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/aab> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Android App Bundle"@en; skos:definition "An Android App Bundle (AAB) is a package file format used by the Android operating system. It includes an app’s compiled code and resources, and defers APK generation and signing to Google Play."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/AAB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "AAB"@en, "AAB"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/aac> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Advanced Audio Coding"@en; skos:definition "Advanced Audio Coding (AAC) is an audio coding standard for lossy digital audio compression. Designed to be the successor of the MP3 format, AAC generally achieves higher sound quality than MP3 at the same bit rate."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/AAC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "AAC"@en, "AAC"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/akn4eu> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Akoma Ntoso file"@en; skos:definition "AKN4EU file is an Akoma Ntoso XML file conforming to the AKN4EU (Akoma Ntoso for European Union) specifications. One or more AKN4EU files can be part of an AKN4EU ZIP file. A special AKN4EU file called ‘main.xml’ is the entry point of an AKN4EU ZIP file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/AKN4EU>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "AKN4EU file"@en, "AKN4EU fail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/akn4eu_leg> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Akoma Ntoso ZIP archive"@en; skos:definition "ZIP archive containing an AKN4EU manifestation of a document in one linguistic variant issued in the legal decision-making process; it must contain at least an AKN4EU file starting with the prefix ‘main-’, which constitutes the entry point, and may contain other associated files and subfolders"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/AKN4EU_LEG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "AKN4EU LEG"@en, "AKN4EU LEG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/akn4eu_zip> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Akoma Ntoso ZIP archive"@en; skos:definition "retired concept; replaced by AKN4EU_LEG"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/AKN4EU_ZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "AKN4EU ZIP"@en, "AKN4EU ZIP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/apk> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Android Package"@en; skos:definition "Android Package (APK) is the package file format used by the Android operating system for distribution and installation of mobile apps, mobile games and middleware."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/APK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "APK"@en, "APK"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/appx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Microsoft AppX application package"@en; skos:definition "AppX is a file format used to distribute and install apps on Windows 8.x and 10, Windows Phone 8.1, Windows 10 Mobile, Xbox One, Hololens and Windows 10 IoT Core."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/APPX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "AppX"@en, "AppX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Internet Archive ARC file format"@en; skos:definition "ARC is the archive file format of Internet Archive. ARC files are large aggregate files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ARC"@en, "ARC"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arc_gz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Compressed Internet Archive ARC file format"@en; skos:definition "ARC is the archive file format of Internet Archive. ARC files are large aggregate files. ARC GZ is ARC compressed by GZIP."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARC_GZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ARC GZ"@en, "ARC GZ"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arcinfo_cov> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ESRI ArcInfo Coverage"@en; skos:definition "An ESRI ArcInfo coverage is a georelational data model that stores vector data – it contains both the spatial (location) and attribute (descriptive) data for geographic features. Coverages use a set of feature classes to represent geographic features. Each feature class stores a set of points, lines (arcs), polygons, or annotation (text). Coverages can have topology, which determines the relationships between features. A coverage is stored as a directory within which each feature class is stored as a set of files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARCINFO_COV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ArcInfo coverage"@en, "ArcInfo coverage"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arff> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Attribute-Relation File Format"@en; skos:definition "ASCII text file that describes a list of instances sharing a set of attributes"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARFF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ARFF"@en, "ARFF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arj> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ARJ archive"@en; skos:definition "Compressed archive file produced by ARJ software. ARJ (Archived by Robert Jung) is a software tool designed by Robert K. Jung for creating high-efficiency compressed file archives."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARJ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ARJ"@en, "ARJ"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arrow_file> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apache Arrow file"@en; skos:definition "Apache columnar format that includes a language-agnostic in-memory data structure specification, metadata serialisation, and a protocol for serialisation and generic data transport; file (random access) format is used for serialising a fixed number of record batches"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARROW_FILE>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Arrow file"@en, "Arrow file"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/arrow_stream> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apache Arrow stream"@en; skos:definition "Apache columnar format that includes a language-agnostic in-memory data structure specification, metadata serialisation, and a protocol for serialisation and generic data transport; streaming format is used for sending an arbitrary length sequence of record batches"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ARROW_STREAM>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Arrow stream"@en, "Arrow stream"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/atom> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Atom Syndication Format"@en; skos:definition "The Atom Feed or Atom Syndication Format is an XML language used for web feeds. Web feeds allow software programs to check for updates published on a website."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ATOM>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Atom Feed"@en, "Atom voog"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/azw> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Amazon Kindle eBook format"@en; skos:definition "AZW Kindle File Format is a proprietary e-book file format created by Amazon.com that can be downloaded and read on devices like smartphones, tablets, computers or e-readers that have Amazon's Kindle application."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/AZW>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Amazon Kindle eBook"@en, "Amazon Kindle e-raamat"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/bin> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "A binary file is a computer file that is not a text file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/BIN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Binary Data"@en, "Binaarsed andmed"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/bits> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Book Interchange Tag Suite"@en; skos:definition "BITS – Book Interchange Tag Suite – is the ‘book version’ of Journal Article Tag Suite (JATS); an XML format used to describe books published online. BITS provides a common XML format in which publishers and archivists can describe textual and graphical content elements. In order to facilitate the reusability, BITS makes a tag set adequate for supporting interchange, archiving, format-conversion and publishing."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/BITS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "BITS XML"@en, "BITS XML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/bmp> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "The bitmap image (BMP) or device independent bitmap (DIB) is a raster graphics image file format used to store bitmap digital images, independently of the display device."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/BMP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Bitmap Image File"@en, "Bitmap pildifail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/bwf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Broadcast Wave File"@en; skos:definition "BWF – Broadcast Wave Format – is an extension of the Microsoft WAV audio format and is the recording format of most file-based non-linear digital recorders used for motion picture, radio and television production. The purpose of this file format is the addition of metadata to facilitate the seamless exchange of sound data between different computer platforms and applications."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/BWF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "BWF"@en, "BWF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/bzip2> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "bzip2 compressed file"@en; skos:definition "An open source, patent- and royalty-free compression format. The compression algorithm is a Burrows-Wheeler transform followed by a move-to-front transform and finally Huffman coding."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/BZIP2>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "bzip2"@en, "bzip2"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/css> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Cascading Style Sheet"@en; skos:definition "CSS – Cascading Style Sheets – is a style sheet language used for describing the presentation of a document written in a markup language."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/CSS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "CSS"@en, "CSS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/csv> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Comma-Separated Values"@en; skos:definition "CSV – comma-separated values – files store tabular data (numbers and text) in plain text. Each line of the file is a data record. Each record consists of one or more fields, separated by commas."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/CSV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "CSV"@en, "CSV"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dapk> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Android Package (Daydream)"@en; skos:definition "An Android Package (APK) with special features used by the Android operating system for the distribution and installation of Daydream mobile apps."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DAPK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DAPK"@en, "DAPK"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dbf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "dBase File"@en; skos:definition "DBF – dBase database file – is supported by a number of database products. dBase was one of the first database management systems for microcomputers."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DBF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DBF"@en, "DBF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dcr> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "DCR is a file type for Adobe Shockwave Media files. DCR files are used to create games and other highly interactive content."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DCR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DCR File"@en, "DCR fail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/deb> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Debian package"@en; skos:definition "Debian package is a standard Unix ar archive that includes two tar archives. One archive holds the control information and another contains the installable data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DEB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "deb"@en, "deb"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dgn> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "DGN file"@en; skos:definition "A DGN file is a 2D/3D drawing created by various construction CAD software, such as MicroStation and Intergraph Interactive Graphics Design System. It may be saved in one of two formats, either the Intergraph Standard File Format (ISFF) or the newer V8 DGN standard. DGN files are typically used to save designs for construction projects for highways, bridges, and buildings."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DGN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DGN"@en, "DGN"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dmg> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apple Disk Image"@en; skos:definition "Apple Disk Image is a disk image format commonly used by the macOS operating system."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DMG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DMG"@en, "DMG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dmp> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "DMP is the media type which shall be used for Oracle dumps. This media type is incomplete as it lacks a reference to the specification of the format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DMP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Oracle Dump"@en, "Oracle Dump"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/doc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Microsoft Word"@en; skos:definition "DOC is a proprietary binary Word document format used by Microsoft Word word processor."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DOC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Word DOC"@en, "Word DOC"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/docx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Office Open XML Document"@en; skos:definition "DOCX is an Office Open XML international standard for Office documents. It is used by Microsoft Word and by a growing number of applications from other vendors in word processing programs."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DOCX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Word DOCX"@en, "Word DOCX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dtd_sgml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "SGML Document Type Definition (DTD)"@en; skos:definition "SGML – Standard Generalized Markup Language – is a standard for defining generalized markup languages for documents. DTD – document type definition – is a set of markup declarations that define a document type for an SGML-family markup language (SGML, XML, HTML). It defines the legal building blocks of an XML document, the document structure with a list of legal elements and attributes."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DTD_SGML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SGML DTD"@en, "SGML DTD"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dtd_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "XML Document Type Definition (DTD)"@en; skos:definition "XML – Extensible Markup Language – is a markup language that defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable. DTD – document type definition – is a set of markup declarations that define a document type for an SGML-family markup language (SGML, XML, HTML). It defines the legal building blocks of an XML document, the document structure with a list of legal elements and attributes. XML uses a subset of SGML DTD."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DTD_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XML DTD"@en, "XML DTD"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dwca> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Darwin Core Archive"@en; skos:definition "biodiversity informatics data standard that makes use of the Darwin Core terms to produce a single, self contained dataset for sharing species-level (taxonomic), species-occurrence data, and sampling-event data; an archive is a set of text files, in standard comma- or tab-delimited format, with a simple descriptor file (called meta.xml) to inform others how the files are organized"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DWCA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DwC-A"@en, "DwC-A"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dwg> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "DWG file"@en; skos:definition "A DWG file is a 2D or 3D drawing created with Autodesk AutoCAD, a professional CAD program. It contains vector image data and metadata that AutoCAD and other CAD applications use to load a drawing. DWG files are related to .DXF files, which are ASCII versions of DWG files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DWG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DWG"@en, "DWG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/dxf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Drawing Interchange Format"@en; skos:definition "A DXF file is a data file saved in a format developed by Autodesk and used for CAD (computer-aided design) vector image files, such as AutoCAD documents. DXF files are similar to .DWG files, but are more compatible with other programs since they are ASCII (text) based."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/DXF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "DXF"@en, "DXF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/e00> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ESRI Arc/Info interchange file"@en; skos:definition "E00 is an ArcInfo interchange file format. ArcInfo is a full-featured geographic information system produced by Esri."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/E00>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "E00"@en, "E00"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ear> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Enterprise Application Archive"@en; skos:definition "EAR (Enterprise Application aRchive) is a file format used by Java EE for packaging one or more modules into a single archive."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/EAR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "EAR"@en, "EAR"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ecw> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Enhanced Compressed Wavelet"@en; skos:definition "ECW – Enhanced Compressed Wavelet – is the media type which shall be used for a proprietary wavelet compression image format optimized for aerial and satellite imagery."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ECW>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ECW"@en, "ECW"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/eforms_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "eForms XML file"@en; skos:definition "EU legislative XML standard for procurement data used by public buyers to publish notices on Tenders Electronic Daily (TED), the European public procurement advertising website. The standard forms (eForms) have been established by the Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/1780 of 23 September 2019, and need to be implemented in national eProcurement systems by being tailored to national needs."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/EFORMS_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "eForms XML"@en, "eForms XML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/eps> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "EPS – Encapsulated PostScript – files are more-or-less self-contained, reasonably predictable PostScript documents that describe an image or drawing and can be placed within another PostScript document."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/EPS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Encapsulated Postscript"@en, "Kapseldatud Postscript"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/epub> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "eBook standard of the International Digital Publishing Forum (IDPF)"@en; skos:definition "EPUB – electronic publication – is an e-book file format that can be downloaded and read on devices like smartphones, tablets, computers or e-readers. It is a technical standard published by the International Digital Publishing Forum (IDPF)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/EPUB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "EPUB"@en, "EPUB"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/etsi_tsl> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ETSI Trusted List"@en; skos:definition "file containing information related to the qualified trust service providers and the qualified trust services provided by them"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ETSI_TSL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ETSI TSL"@en, "ETSI TSL"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/etsi_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "European Telecommunications Standards Institute signature validation report XML"@en; skos:definition "ETSI signature validation report is a European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI) signature validation report XML file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ETSI_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ETSI signature validation report"@en, "ETSI signature validation report"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/exe> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Executable file"@en; skos:definition "An executable file (the main execution point of a computer program) for DOS, OpenVMS, Microsoft Windows, Symbian or OS/2. Besides the executable program, many .exe files contain other components called resources, such as bitmap graphics and icons which the executable program may use for its graphical user interface."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/EXE>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "EXE"@en, "EXE"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/fmx2> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Formalized Exchange of Electronic Publications (Formex), version 2"@en; skos:definition "Formex describes the format for the exchange of data between the Publication Office and its contractors. In particular, it defines the logical markup for documents which are published in the different series of the Offical Journal of the European Union. Formex 2 was a previous version of Formex actually used."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/FMX2>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Formex 2"@en, "Formex 2"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/fmx3> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Formalized Exchange of Electronic Publications (Formex), version 3"@en; skos:definition "Formex describes the format for the exchange of data between the Publication Office and its contractors. In particular, it defines the logical markup for documents which are published in the different series of the Offical Journal of the European Union. Formex 3 was a previous version of Formex actually used."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/FMX3>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Formex 3"@en, "Formex 3"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/fmx4> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Formalized Exchange of Electronic Publications (Formex), version 4"@en; skos:definition "Formex describes the format for the exchange of data between the Publication Office and its contractors. In particular, it defines the logical markup for documents which are published in the different series of the Offical Journal of the European Union. Formex V4 is based on the international standard XML."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/FMX4>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Formex 4"@en, "Formex 4"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/fmx4_zip> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Formex 4 ZIP archive"@en; skos:definition "FMX4 ZIP is a ZIP archive containing files that all belong to a Formex 4 instance."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/FMX4_ZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "FMX4 ZIP"@en, "FMX4 ZIP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gdb> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Environmental Systems Research Institute File Geodatabase"@en; skos:definition "GDB is an Esri's file-based geodatabase format, stored as folders in a file system. It shall be used for Esri file geodatabases. The file is a zip archive that contains the gdb directory."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GDB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Esri File Geodatabase"@en, "Esri File geoandmebaas"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/geojson> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Geographical JavaScript Object Notation"@en; skos:definition "GeoJSON is an open standard format designed for representing simple geographical features, along with their non-spatial attributes, based on JSON."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GEOJSON>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GeoJSON"@en, "GeoJSON"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/geotiff> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "OGC GeoTIFF"@en; skos:definition "GeoTIFF is a public domain metadata standard which allows georeferencing information to be embedded within a TIFF file. The potential additional information includes map projection, coordinate systems, ellipsoids, datums, and everything else necessary to establish the exact spatial reference for the file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GEOTIFF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GeoTIFF"@en, "GeoTIFF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gif> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Graphics Interchange Format"@en; skos:definition "GIF – Graphics Interchange Format – is a bitmap image format that was developed by a team at the bulletin board service (BBS) provider CompuServe."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GIF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GIF"@en, "GIF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Geography Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "GML – Geography Markup Language – is the XML grammar defined by the Open Geospatial Consortium (OGC) to express geographical features. GML serves as a modeling language for geographic systems as well as an open interchange format for geographic transactions on the Internet."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GML"@en, "GML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gmz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Zipped Geography Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "GMZ is the media type which shall be used for a zip archive that contains one or more GML documents."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GMZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Zipped GML"@en, "Tihendatud GML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gpkg> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "OGC GeoPackage"@en; skos:definition "An OGC GeoPackage is an open, standards-based, platform-independent, portable, self-describing, compact format for transferring geospatial information. It is implemented as a SQLite database container."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GPKG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GeoPackage"@en, "GeoPackage"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gpx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "GPS Exchange Format"@en; skos:definition "light-weight XML data format for the interchange of GPS data (waypoints, routes, and tracks) between applications and web services"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GPX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GPX"@en, "GPX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/grid> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Environmental Systems Research Institute binary grid"@en; skos:definition "Esri binary grid is a proprietary binary variation of an Esri grid, a raster GIS file format developed by Esri. It is also known as an ARC/INFO GRID or ARC GRID. It differs from the other Esri grid variation, a non-proprietary ASCII format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GRID>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Esri binary grid"@en, "Esri binaarne ruutkava"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/grid_ascii> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Environmental Systems Research Institute ASCII grid"@en; skos:definition "Esri ASCII grid is the media type which shall be used for ASCII GRID files. ASCII GRID is one of the two formats of Esri grid, a raster GIS file format, a non-proprietary ASCII format, also known as an ArcInfo ASCII GRID."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GRID_ASCII>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Esri ASCII grid"@en, "Esri ASCII ruutkava"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gtfs> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "General Transit Feed Specification"@en; skos:definition "The General Transit Feed Specification (GTFS) is a data specification that allows public transit agencies to publish their transit data in a format that can be consumed by a wide variety of software applications. GTFS is split into a schedule component that contains schedule, fare, and geographic transit information and a real-time component that contains arrival predictions, vehicle positions and service advisories."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GTFS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GTFS"@en, "GTFS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/gzip> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "GZIP – GNU zip – is a file format and a software application used for file compression and decompression."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "GNU zip"@en, "GNU zip"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/hdf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Hierarchical Data Format"@en; skos:definition "HDF is a set of file formats (HDF4, HDF5) designed to store and organize large amounts of numerical data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HDF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "HDF"@en, "HDF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/hdt> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Header Dictionary Triples"@en; skos:definition "HDT (Header, Dictionary, Triples) is a compact data structure and binary serialization format for Resource Description Framework (RDF) that keeps big datasets compressed to save space while maintaining search and browse operations without prior decompression."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HDT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "HDT"@en, "HDT"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/html> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "HyperText Mark-up Language"@en; skos:definition "HTML is the standard markup language used to create web pages and its elements form the building blocks of all websites."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HTML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "HTML"@en, "HTML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/html5> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "HyperText Mark-up Language 5"@en; skos:definition "HTML5 is a markup language used for structuring and presenting content on the World Wide Web. It is the fifth and last major HTML version that is a World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) recommendation. The current specification is known as the HTML Living Standard. It is maintained by the Web Hypertext Application Technology Working Group (WHATWG), a consortium of the major browser vendors (Apple, Google, Mozilla, and Microsoft)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HTML5>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "HTML5"@en, "HTML5"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/html_simpl> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "HyperText Mark-up Language, simplified"@en; skos:definition "HTML is a markup language for describing web documents. Its simplified version is used for storage in the Publications Office."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HTML_SIMPL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "HTML simplified"@en, "HTML lihtsustatud"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ics> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "iCalendar"@en; skos:definition "iCalendar is a computer file format which allows Internet users to send meeting requests and tasks to other Internet users by sharing or sending files in this format through various methods."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ICS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ICalendar"@en, "IKalender"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/immc_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Files exchanged within the context of the Interinstitutional Metadata Maintenance Committee (IMMC) communication protocol."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/IMMC_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "IMMC XML message"@en, "IMMC XML sõnum"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/indd> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Adobe InDesign Document"@en; skos:definition "INDD is a file format for a page layout file used by Adobe InDesign. InDesign is a desktop publishing software application."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/INDD>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "INDD"@en, "INDD"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ipa> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "iOS App Store Package"@en; skos:definition "An .ipa (iOS App Store Package) file is an application archive file used by the iOS operating system."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/IPA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "IPA"@en, "IPA"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/iso> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ISO Disc Image file"@en; skos:definition "Archive file containing the content from (or destined for) an optical disk. Originally it was limited to data formatted to comply with the ISO 9660 standard (1988), hence the format name and the iso file extension. The ISO Disk Image File Format is typically used to package or bundle software, databases, authored DVD video programs, and the like. ISO image files, unlike normal files, are not opened but rather are mounted. ISO image files contain the data contents of every written sector of an optical disc, including the optical disc file system if one is present."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ISO>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ISO image"@en, "ISO pilt"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/iso_zip> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Zipped ISO Disc Image file"@en; skos:definition "ZIP archive containing an ISO disc image file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ISO_ZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Zipped ISO image"@en, "Tihendatud ISO pilt"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/jar> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Java Archive"@en; skos:definition "JAR (Java Archive) is an archive file that includes a Java-specific manifest file. It is built on the ZIP format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JAR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JAR"@en, "JAR"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/jats> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Journal Article Tag Suite"@en; skos:definition "JATS – Journal Article Tag Suite – is an XML format used to describe scientific literature published online. It is a technical standard developed by the National Information Standards Organization (NISO)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JATS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JATS XML"@en, "JATS XML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/jpeg> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "JPEG – Joint Photographic Experts Group – is a commonly used method of lossy compression for digital images, particularly for those images produced by digital photography. The degree of compression can be adjusted, allowing a selectable tradeoff between storage size and image quality."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JPEG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JPEG"@en, "JPEG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/jpeg2000> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Joint Photographic Experts Group 2000"@en; skos:definition "JPEG 2000 – Joint Photographic Experts Group 2000 – is an image coding system that uses state-of-the-art compression techniques based on wavelet technology."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JPEG2000>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JPEG 2000"@en, "JPEG 2000"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/js> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "JavaScript is a high-level, interpreted programming language. It is a language which is also characterized as dynamic, weakly typed, prototype-based and multi-paradigm."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JavaScript"@en, "JavaScript"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/json> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "JavaScript Object Notation"@en; skos:definition "JSON is an open-standard file format that uses human-readable text to transmit data objects consisting of attribute–value pairs and array data types (or any other serializable value). It is a very common data format used for asynchronous browser/server communication."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JSON>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JSON"@en, "JSON"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/json_ld> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data"@en; skos:definition "JSON-LD is a JSON-based format to serialize Linked Data. It is primarily intended to be a way to use Linked Data in Web-based programming environments, to build interoperable Web services, and to store Linked Data in JSON-based storage engines."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/JSON_LD>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "JSON-LD"@en, "JSON-LD"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/kml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Keyhole Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "KML – Keyhole Markup Language – is an XML notation for expressing geographic annotation and visualization within Internet-based, two-dimensional maps and three-dimensional Earth browsers. KML was developed for use with Google Earth and became an international standard."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/KML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "KML"@en, "KML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/kmz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Keyhole Markup Language, Zipped"@en; skos:definition "A KMZ file consists of a main KML file and zero or more supporting files that are packaged using a Zip utility into one unit, called an archive. The KMZ file can then be stored and emailed as a single entity. A NetworkLink can fetch a KMZ file from a web server. When the KMZ file is unzipped, the main .kml file and its supporting files are separated into their original formats and directory structure, with their original filenames and extensions. In addition to being an archive format, the Zip format is also compressed, so an archive can include only a single large KML file. Depending on the content of the KML file, this process typically results in 10:1 compression. Your 10 Kbyte KML file can be served with a 1 Kbyte KMZ file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/KMZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "KMZ"@en, "KMZ"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/las> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "LAS – LASer file format – is the media type which shall be used for a public file format for the interchange of 3-dimensional point cloud data data between data users."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LAS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "LASer file"@en, "LASer fail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/laz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Compressed LASer file"@en; skos:definition "LAZ is the media type which shall be used for compressed LAS files. This media type is incomplete as it lacks a reference to the specification of the format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LAZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Compressed LAS file"@en, "Kompressitud LAS fail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/leg> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "retired concept; see AKN4EU_LEG"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LEG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "LEG"@en, "LEG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/legalhtml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "LegalHTML file"@en; skos:definition "extension of the HTML language designed for representing legal acts; it provides an explicit domain language addressing all structural aspects of an act such as articles, paragraphs, items and references; it also supports the description of the editorial and jurisdictional history of an act and the semantic annotation of domain entities; furthermore, LegalHTML addresses the consolidation of an act and its subsequent modifications into a single document using a tree-like representation of the original content and of its modified versions; finally, a JavaScript API enhances the representation as an active document, enabling the visualization of a consolidated act as it applies at different points in time"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LEGALHTML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "LegalHTML"@en, "LegalHTML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/lha> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "LHA compressed file"@en; skos:definition "Compressed file produced by LHA, a freeware compression utility."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LHA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "LHA"@en, "LHA"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/lpk> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ArcGIS layer package"@en; skos:definition "A layer package packages one or more layers and all referenced data sources to create a single compressed .lpk file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LPK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Layer package"@en, "Layer package"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/lzip> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "lzip compressed file"@en; skos:definition "Compressed file produced by lzip, free, command-line tool for the compression of data that employs the Lempel-Ziv-Markov chain algorithm (LZMA)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "lzip"@en, "lzip"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/lzma> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "lzma compressed file"@en; skos:definition "Compressed file produced using LZMA (Lempel-Ziv-Markov) chain algorithm."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LZMA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "lzma"@en, "lzma"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/lzo> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "lzo compressed file"@en; skos:definition "Compressed file produced using LZO (Lempel-Ziv-Oberhumer), a lossless data compression algorithm that is focused on decompression speed."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/LZO>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "lzo"@en, "lzo"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/map_prvw> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Esri's ArcGIS is a geographic information system (GIS) for working with maps and geographic information. Map previews are normal raster background maps."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MAP_PRVW>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ArcGIS Map Preview"@en, "ArcGIS Map eelvaade"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/map_srvc> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Esri's ArcGIS is a geographic information system (GIS) for working with maps and geographic information. Map services offer access to map and layer content."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MAP_SRVC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ArcGIS Map Service"@en, "ArcGIS Map teenus"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/markdown> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Markdown file"@en; skos:definition "lightweight markup language for creating formatted text using a plain-text editor"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MARKDOWN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Markdown"@en, "Markdown"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mathml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Mathematical Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "mathematical markup language, an application of XML for describing mathematical notations and capturing both its structure and content"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MATHML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MathML"@en, "MathML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/matlab_mat> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "MATLAB MAT-File"@en; skos:definition "proprietary, binary data container format used by MATLAB software from MathWorks"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MATLAB_MAT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MATLAB MAT"@en, "MATLAB MAT"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mbox> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Mbox"@en; skos:definition "MBOX is a generic term for a family of related file formats used for holding collections of email messages. All messages in an mbox mailbox are concatenated and stored as plain text in a single file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MBOX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MBOX"@en, "MBOX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mdb> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Microsoft Access Database"@en; skos:definition "MDB – Microsoft Database – is a proprietary file format used by 2003 and earlier versions of Microsoft Access. Microsoft Access is a database management system."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MDB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MDB"@en, "MDB"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mets> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Metadata Encoding and Transmission Standard – Logical METS container"@en; skos:definition "METS – Metadata Encoding and Transmission Standard – is a metadata standard for encoding descriptive, administrative and structural metadata regarding objects within a digital library, expressed using the XML schema language."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/METS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "METS XML"@en, "METS XML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mets_zip> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Metadata Encoding and Transmission Standard – Physical METS container"@en; skos:definition "METS package is a zip file containing METS XML files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/METS_ZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "METS package"@en, "METS pakett"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mhtml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "MIME HTML"@en; skos:definition "MHTML – MIME Encapsulation of Aggregate HTML Documents – is a web page archive format used to combine in a single document the HTML code and its companion resources that are otherwise represented by external links (such as images, Flash animations, Java applets and audio files). The content of an MHTML file is encoded as if it were an HTML e-mail message."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MHTML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MHTML"@en, "MHTML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mif_mid> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "MapInfo interchange format"@en; skos:definition "MapInfo interchange format is a map and database exporting file format of MapInfo software product. The MIF-file filename usually ends with .mif-suffix. Some MIF-files also have a related MID-file. The filename of a MID-file usually ends with .mid-suffix."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MIF_MID>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MIF/MID"@en, "MIF/MID"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mobi> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Mobipocket eBook format"@en; skos:definition "Mobipocket eBook is a proprietary e-book file format of Mobipocket SA company that can be used by mobile phones, personal digital assistants (PDA) and desktop operating systems."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MOBI>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Mobipocket eBook"@en, "Mobipocket e-raamat"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mop> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "MOPAC Input Format"@en; skos:definition "MOP is a chemical file format used by MOPAC. MOPAC is a popular computer program used in computational chemistry. It is designed to implement semi-empirical quantum chemistry algorithms."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MOP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MOP"@en, "MOP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mov> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "QuickTime Movie"@en; skos:definition "computer file format used natively by the QuickTime framework; the format specifies a multimedia container file that contains one or more tracks, each of which stores a particular type of data: audio, video, or text (e.g. for subtitles)"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MOV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MOV"@en, "MOV"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mp3> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "MPEG-1/MPEG-2 Audio Layer III"@en; skos:definition "An MP3 is a format for digital audio. It uses the lossy compression to reduce the data without losing audio quality."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MP3>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MP3"@en, "MP3"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mpeg2> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Moving Picture Experts Group 2"@en; skos:definition "MPEG-2 – Moving Picture Experts Group – is a standard for the generic coding of moving pictures and associated audio information. It describes a combination of lossy video compression and lossy audio data compression methods, which permit storage and transmission of movies using currently available storage media and transmission bandwidth."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MPEG2>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MPEG-2"@en, "MPEG-2"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mpeg4> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Moving Picture Experts Group 4"@en; skos:definition "MPEG-4 – Moving Picture Experts Group – is a method of defining compression of audio and visual (AV) digital data. It was designated a standard for a group of audio and video coding formats and related technology."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MPEG4>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MPEG-4"@en, "MPEG-4"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mpeg4_avc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Moving Picture Experts Group 4 Advanced Video Coding"@en; skos:definition "MPEG-4 – Moving Picture Experts Group – Part 10, Advanced Video Coding is a block-oriented motion-compensation-based video compression standard. It is one of the most commonly used formats for the recording, compression and distribution of video content."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MPEG4_AVC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MPEG-4 AVC"@en, "MPEG-4 AVC"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mrsid> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Multiresolution seamless image database"@en; skos:definition "Multiresolution seamless image database (MrSID) is a file format developed and patented by LizardTech for encoding of georeferenced raster graphics, such as orthophotos. With this format, large raster image files such as aerial photographs or satellite imagery are compressed and can be quickly viewed without having to decompress the entire file."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MRSID>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MrSID"@en, "MrSID"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/msg_http> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "HTTP Message Syntax and Routing"@en; skos:definition "HTTP – Hypertext Transfer Protocol – is a stateless application-level request/response protocol that uses extensible semantics and self-descriptive message payloads for flexible interaction with network-based hypertext information systems. Message Syntax and Routing is part of the HTTP/1.1 specification."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MSG_HTTP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "HTTP Message"@en, "HTTP sõnum"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/msi> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Windows Installer Package"@en; skos:definition "Archive file for Windows Installer containing the installation information and an optional .cab file payload."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MSI>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MSI"@en, "MSI"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/mxd> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ArcGIS Map Document"@en; skos:definition "MXD – Map Exchange Document – is a file format in which the maps created from ArcGIS software can be stored."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/MXD>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MXD"@en, "MXD"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/n3> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Notation3"@en; skos:definition "Non-XML serialization of Resource Description Framework models."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/N3>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "N3"@en, "N3"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/netcdf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Network Common Data Form"@en; skos:definition "NetCDF is a set of software libraries and self-describing, machine-independent data formats that support the creation, access and sharing of array-oriented scientific data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/NETCDF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "NetCDF"@en, "NetCDF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/oapk> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Android Package (Oculus)"@en; skos:definition "An Android Package (APK) with special features used by the Android operating system for the distribution and installation of Oculus mobile apps."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/OAPK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OAPK"@en, "OAPK"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/octet> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Octet is the Internet media type for an arbitrary byte stream. A byte streamor octet stream is a series of bytes."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/OCTET>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Octet Stream"@en, "Octet voog"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/odb> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "OpenDocument is a standardized Open Document Format for Office Applications. Databases are organized collections of data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OpenDocument Database"@en, "OpenDocument andmebaas"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/odc> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "OpenDocument is a standardized Open Document Format for Office Applications. Charts define how to create graphical displays from numerical data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OpenDocument Chart"@en, "OpenDocument graafik"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/odf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "OpenDocument Format"@en; skos:definition "ODF – Open Document Format for Office Applications, also known as OpenDocument – is an XML-based file format for spreadsheets, charts, presentations and word processing documents. It was developed with the aim of providing an open, XML-based file format specification for office applications."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ODF"@en, "ODF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/odg> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "OpenDocument is a standardized Open Document Format for Office Applications. Image files are composed of digital data and are used to organize and store digital images."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OpenDocument Image"@en, "OpenDocument pilt"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/odp> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "OpenDocument Presentation"@en; skos:definition "ODP is an OpenDocument file format for presentations. OpenDocument was developed with the aim of providing an open, XML-based file format specification for office applications."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ODP"@en, "ODP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ods> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "OpenDocument Spreadsheet"@en; skos:definition "ODS is an OpenDocument file format for spreadsheets. OpenDocument was developed with the aim of providing an open, XML-based file format specification for office applications."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ODS"@en, "ODS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/odt> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Open Document Text"@en; skos:definition "ODT is the word processing file format of OpenDocument, an open standard for electronic documents."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ODT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ODT"@en, "ODT"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ogcfeat> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "OGC API Features"@en; skos:definition "multi-part standard that offers the capability to create, modify, and query spatial data on the Web and specifies requirements and recommendations for APIs that want to follow a standard way of sharing feature data"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/OGCFEAT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OGCFeat"@en, "OGCFeat"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/op_datpro> a skos:Concept; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/OP_DATPRO>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Неокончателни данни"@bg, "Předběžné údaje"@cs, "Midlertidige data"@da, "Vorläufige Daten"@de, "Προσωρινά δεδομένα"@el, "Provisional data"@en, "Datos provisionales"@es, "Esialgsed andmed"@et, "Alustavat tiedot"@fi, "Données provisoires"@fr, "Sonraí sealadacha"@ga, "Privremeni podaci"@hr, "Ideiglenes adatok"@hu, "Dati provvisori"@it, "Laikinieji duomenys"@lt, "Provizoriski dati"@lv, "Dejta provviżorja"@mt, "Voorlopige gegevens"@nl, "Dane tymczasowe"@pl, "Dados provisórios"@pt, "Date provizorii"@ro, "Predbežné údaje"@sk, "Začasni podatki"@sl, "Tillfälliga uppgifter"@sv .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ovf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Open Virtualization Format"@en; skos:definition "OVF – Open Virtualization Format – is an open standard for packaging and distributing virtual appliances or more generally software to be run in virtual machines."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/OVF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OVF"@en, "OVF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/owl> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Ontology Language"@en; skos:definition "OWL – Web Ontology Language – is a family of knowledge representation languages for authoring ontologies."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/OWL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "OWL"@en, "OWL"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/parquet> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apache Parquet file"@en; skos:definition "Apache columnar storage format available to any project in the Hadoop ecosystem, regardless of the choice of data processing framework, data model or programming language; explicitly designed to separate the metadata from the data"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PARQUET>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Parquet"@en, "Parquet"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Portable Document Format"@en; skos:definition "PDF – Portable Document Format – is a file format developed to present documents, including text formatting and images, in a manner independent of application software, hardware and operating systems. Based on the PostScript language, each PDF file encapsulates a complete description of a fixed-layout flat document, including the text, fonts, vector graphics, raster images and other information needed to display it. PDF was standardized as an open format and does not require any royalties for its implementation."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF"@en, "PDF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdf1x> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PDF printing format extension"@en; skos:definition "PDF1X is a PDF specification used mainly for high quality color printing."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDF1X>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF1X"@en, "PDF1X"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa1a> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PDF archiving format, Level A conformance"@en; skos:definition "PDF/A-1 is the Part 1 of the PDF standard and specifies two levels of conformance for PDF files. PDF/A-1a – Level A (accessible) conformance was intended to increase the accessibility of conforming files for physically impaired users by allowing assistive software, such as screen readers, to more precisely extract and interpret a file's contents."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA1A>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-1a"@en, "PDF/A-1a"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa1b> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PDF archiving format, Level B conformance"@en; skos:definition "PDF/A-1 is the Part 1 of the PDF standard and specifies two levels of conformance for PDF files. Level B (basic) conformance requires only that standards necessary for the reliable reproduction of a document's visual appearance be followed."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA1B>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-1b"@en, "PDF/A-1b"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa2a> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/A-2 is the Part 2 of the PDF standard and specifies three levels of conformance for PDF files. PDF/A-2a corresponds to conformance level a in PDF/A-1 (accessible)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA2A>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-2a"@en, "PDF/A-2a"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa2b> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/A-2 is the Part 2 of the PDF standard and specifies three levels of conformance for PDF files. PDF/A-2b corresponds to conformance level a in PDF/A-2 (basic)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA2B>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-2b"@en, "PDF/A-2b"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa3> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "ISO-standardised version of the Portable Document Format specialized for use in the archiving and long-term preservation of electronic documents; PDF/A-3 is the Part 3 of the standard which differs from PDF/A-2 in only one regard – it allows embedding of arbitrary file formats (such as XML, CSV, CAD, word-processing documents, spreadsheet documents and others) into PDF/A conforming documents"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA3>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-3"@en, "PDF/A-3"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa3a> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/A-3 subtype ensuring both accessibility and structure preservation, similar to PDF/A-2a"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA3A>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-3a"@en, "PDF/A-3a"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa3b> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/A-3 subtype that guarantees visual fidelity without regard for structure"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA3B>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-3b"@en, "PDF/A-3b"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfa3u> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/A-3 subtype that supports Unicode, ensuring that non-Latin text is correctly represented"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFA3U>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/A-3u"@en, "PDF/A-3u"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfua> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PDF/Universal Accessibility"@en; skos:definition "PDF/UA (PDF/Universal Accessibility), formally ISO 14289, is an International Organization for Standardization (ISO) standard for accessible PDF technology. A technical specification intended for developers implementing PDF writing and processing software, PDF/UA provides definitive terms and requirements for accessibility in PDF documents and applications. For those equipped with appropriate software, conformance with PDF/UA ensures accessibility for people with disabilities who use assistive technology such as screen readers, screen magnifiers, joysticks and other technologies to navigate and read electronic content."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFUA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/UA"@en, "PDF/UA"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PDF printing format, Blind eXchange"@en; skos:definition "PDF/X is a subset of the PDF standard. The purpose of PDF/X is to facilitate graphics exchange, and it therefore has a series of printing related requirements which do not apply to standard PDF files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/X"@en, "PDF/X"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfx1a> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/X-1a is a PDF specification which completes exchange using CMYK data and spots colour printing data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFX1A>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/X-1a"@en, "PDF/X-1a"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfx2a> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/X-2a is a PDF specification in which colour-managed, CMYK and spot colour data are supported in any combination."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFX2A>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/X-2a"@en, "PDF/X-2a"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pdfx4> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "PDF/X-4 is a PDF specification in which colour-managed, CMYK, gray, RGB or spot colour data are supported, as are PDF transparency and optional content."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PDFX4>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PDF/X-4"@en, "PDF/X-4"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pl> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Source code written in the Perl programming language."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Perl script"@en, "Perl script"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/png> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Portable Network Graphics"@en; skos:definition "PNG – Portable Network Graphics – is a raster graphics file format that supports lossless data compression. PNG was created as an improved, non-patented replacement for Graphics Interchange Format (GIF), and is the most widely used lossless image compression format on the Internet."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PNG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PNG"@en, "PNG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pps> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Microsoft PowerPoint Slide Show"@en; skos:definition "PPS – PowerPoint 97–2003 binary slide show – is a binary filaname extension of Microsoft PowerPoint presentation program. PowerPoint was originally designed to provide visuals for group presentations within business organizations, but has come to be very widely used in many other communication situations, both in business and beyond."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PPS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PowerPoint Slide Show"@en, "PowerPoint slaidiesitlus"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ppsx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PowerPoint Open XML Slide Show"@en; skos:definition "PPSX – PowerPoint 2007 XML slide show – is an XML filename extension of Microsoft PowerPoint presentation program. PowerPoint was originally designed to provide visuals for group presentations within business organizations, but has come to be very widely used in many other communication situations, both in business and beyond."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PPSX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PowerPoint PPSX"@en, "PowerPoint PPSX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ppt> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Microsoft PowerPoint Presentation"@en; skos:definition "PPT is a binary media type of Microsoft PowerPoint presentation program. PowerPoint was originally designed to provide visuals for group presentations within business organizations, but has come to be very widely used in many other communication situations, both in business and beyond."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PPT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PowerPoint PPT"@en, "PowerPoint PPT"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pptx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Office Open XML Presentation"@en; skos:definition "PPTX – PowerPoint 2007 XML presentation – is an XML filename extension of Office Open XML version of Microsoft PowerPoint presentation program. PowerPoint was originally designed to provide visuals for group presentations within business organizations, but has come to be very widely used in many other communication situations, both in business and beyond."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PPTX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PowerPoint PPTX"@en, "PowerPoint PPTX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ps> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "PostScript File"@en; skos:definition "PS – PostScript – is a page description language in the electronic publishing and desktop publishing business. It is a dynamically typed, concatenative programming language."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PS"@en, "PS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/psd> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Adobe Photoshop Document"@en; skos:definition "PSD – Photoshop Document – stores an image with support for most imaging options available in Adobe Photoshop. Photoshop is a raster graphics editor."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PSD>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PSD"@en, "PSD"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/pwp> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Packaged Web Publications"@en; skos:definition "Transmitting, storing, sharing or archiving a web publication is easier if it can be packaged as a single file. A Web Publication (WP) is a collection of one or more constituent resources, organized together in a uniquely identifiable grouping that may be presented using standard Open Web Platform technologies. A Packaged Web Publication (PWP) is a Web Publication whose constituent resources are combined into a single distributable file, using some standard packaging format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PWP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "PWP"@en, "PWP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/qgs> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Quantum GIS project"@en; skos:definition "QGS file is a Quantum GIS project. Quantum GIS (QGIS) is a cross-platform free and open source desktop geographic information systems (GIS) application that provides data viewing, editing, and analysis capabilities."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/QGS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "QGS"@en, "QGS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rar> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Roshal Archive"@en; skos:definition "RAR is a proprietary archive file format that supports data compression, error recovery and file spanning."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RAR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RAR"@en, "RAR"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdata> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "R Data format"@en; skos:definition "open source data format of the statistical computing and graphic software R"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDATA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RData"@en, "RData"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Resource Description Framework (RDF)"@en; skos:definition "RDF – Resource Description Framework – is a standard model for data interchange on the Web. RDF has features that facilitate data merging. RDF extends the linking structure of the Web to use URIs to name the relationship between things as well as the two ends of the link (this is usually referred to as a ‘triple’). Using this simple model, it allows structured and semi-structured data to be mixed, exposed and shared across different applications. This linking structure forms a directed, labeled graph, where the edges represent the named link between two resources, represented by the graph nodes."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF"@en, "RDF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_n_quads> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Resource Description Framework N-Quads"@en; skos:definition "N-Quads is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF dataset. N-quads statements are a sequence of RDF terms representing the subject, predicate, object and graph label of an RDF Triple and the graph it is part of in a dataset."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_N_QUADS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF N-Quads"@en, "RDF N-Quads"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_n_triples> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Resource Description Framework N-Triples"@en; skos:definition "RDF N-Triples is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF graph; a concrete syntax for RDF, an easy to parse line-based subset of Turtle."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_N_TRIPLES>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF N-Triples"@en, "RDF N-Triples"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_thrift> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "RDF Binary Thrift"@en; skos:definition "RDF Binary using Apache Thrift (‘RDF Thrift’) is a binary format for RDF and RDF-related data. Binary formats are faster to process – they do not incur the parsing costs of text-base formats. RDF Thrift defines basic encoding for RDF terms, then builds data formats for RDF graphs, RDF datasets and for SPARQL result sets. This gives a basis for high-performance linked data systems."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_THRIFT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF Thrift"@en, "RDF Thrift"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_trig> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Resource Description Framework TriG"@en; skos:definition "TriG allows an RDF dataset to be completely written in a compact and natural text form, with abbreviations for common usage patterns and datatypes. TriG is an extension of the Turtle format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_TRIG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF TriG"@en, "RDF TriG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_trix> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Triples in XML"@en; skos:definition "TriX (Triples in XML) is a serialization format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs. It is an XML format for serializing Named Graphs and RDF Datasets which offers a compact and readable alternative to the XML-based RDF/XML syntax."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_TRIX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF TriX"@en, "RDF TriX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_turtle> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Terse RDF Triple Language"@en; skos:definition "Turtle – Terse RDF Triple Language – is a format for expressing data in the Resource Description Framework (RDF) data model with a syntax similar to SPARQL. RDF, in turn, represents information using ‘triples’, each of which consists of a subject, a predicate and an object. Each of those items is expressed as a Web URI."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_TURTLE>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF Turtle"@en, "RDF Turtle"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdf_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Resource Description Framework XML syntax"@en; skos:definition "RDF XML is a syntax, defined by the W3C, to express (i.e. serialize) an RDF graph as an XML document."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDF XML"@en, "RDF XML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rdfa> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Resource Description Framework in Attributes"@en; skos:definition "RDFa is a technique that provides a set of markup attributes to augment the visual information on the Web with machine-readable hints."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDFA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RDFa"@en, "RDFa"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rest> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Esri Representational State Transfer"@en; skos:definition "Esri REST is a standard way for web clients to communicate with geographic information system (GIS) servers through Representational State Transfer (REST) technology."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/REST>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Esri REST"@en, "Esri REST"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rpm> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "RPM Package"@en; skos:definition "File format for RPM Package Manager (originally Red Hat Package Manager), free and open-source package management system."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RPM>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RPM"@en, "RPM"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rss> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Really Simple Syndication"@en; skos:definition "RSS – Rich Site Summary; originally RDF Site Summary; often called Really Simple Syndication – is a type of web feed which allows users to access updates to online content in a standardized, computer-readable format. These feeds can, for example, allow a user to keep track of many different websites in a single news aggregator. Websites usually use RSS feeds to publish frequently updated information, such as blog entries, news headlines, audio, video. An RSS document (called ‘feed’, ‘web feed’ or ‘channel’) includes full or summarized text and metadata."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RSS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RSS feed"@en, "RSS feed"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/rtf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Rich Text Format File"@en; skos:definition "RTF – Rich Text Format – is a proprietary document file format developed for cross-platform document interchange with Microsoft products."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RTF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "RTF"@en, "RTF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sas> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "SAS dataset"@en; skos:definition "proprietary data format of the statistical analysis software SAS"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SAS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SAS"@en, "SAS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sb3> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Scratch 3.0"@en; skos:definition "Scratch 3.0 is a file format used to store exported Scratch 3.0 projects and sprites. These are ZIP archives which contain information encoded in a text-based JSON format and project media in separate files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SB3>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "sb3"@en, "sb3"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sch> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Schematron file"@en; skos:definition "rule-based validation language for making assertions about the structure and content of XML documents; it is expressed in XML using a small number of elements and XPath; it has been standardised as part of ISO/IEC 19757"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SCH>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Schematron"@en, "Schematron"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/schema_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "XML Schema"@en; skos:definition "An XML schema is a description of a type of XML document, typically expressed in terms of constraints on the structure and content of documents of that type, above and beyond the basic syntactical constraints imposed by XML itself."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SCHEMA_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XML schema"@en, "XML skeem"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sdmx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Statistical Data and Metadata eXchange"@en; skos:definition "SDMX is an initiative to foster standards for the exchange of statistical information. The SDMX message formats have two basic expressions, SDMX-ML (using XML syntax) and SDMX-EDI (using EDIFACT syntax and based on the GESMES/TS statistical message)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SDMX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SDMX"@en, "SDMX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sgml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Standard Generalized Mark-up Language"@en; skos:definition "SGML – Standard Generalized Markup Language – is a standard for defining generalized markup languages for documents. Generalized markup is based on two postulates: markup should be declarative and rigorous."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SGML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SGML"@en, "SGML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/shp> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Environmental Systems Research Institute Shape"@en; skos:definition "SHP – shapefile format – is a popular geospatial vector data format for geographic information system (GIS) software. Esri shapefile is a zip archive that contains at least the shp, shx and dbf files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SHP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Esri Shape"@en, "Esri Shape"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/skos_xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Simple Knowledge Organization System"@en; skos:definition "SKOS – Simple Knowledge Organization System – is a W3C recommendation designed for representation of thesauri, classification schemes, taxonomies, subject-heading systems or any other type of structured controlled vocabulary. XML – Extensible Markup Language – is a markup language that defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SKOS_XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SKOS"@en, "SKOS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sparqlq> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "SPARQL Query"@en; skos:definition "SPARQL – a recursive acronym for SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language – is an RDF query language, that is, a semantic query language for databases, able to retrieve and manipulate data stored in Resource Description Framework (RDF) format. It is recognised as one of the key technologies of the semantic web."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SPARQLQ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SPARQL"@en, "SPARQL"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sparqlqres> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "SPARQL Query Results"@en; skos:definition "Results of a SPARQL query. SPARQL – SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language – is an RDF query language, that is, a semantic query language for databases, able to retrieve and manipulate data stored in Resource Description Framework (RDF) format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SPARQLQRES>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SPARQL results"@en, "SPARQL tulemused"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/spss_sav> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "SPSS Statistics file"@en; skos:definition "proprietary data format of the statistical software SPSS"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SPSS_SAV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SPSS SAV"@en .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/sql> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Structured Query Language"@en; skos:definition "SQL – Structured Query Language – is a domain-specific language used in programming and designed for managing data held in a relational database management system (RDBMS) or for stream processing in a relational data stream management system (RDSMS)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SQL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SQL"@en, "SQL"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/stata_dta> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Stata dataset"@en; skos:definition "proprietary data format of the statistical software Stata"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/STATA_DTA>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Stata DTA"@en, "Stata DTA"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/stl> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "StereoLithography"@en; skos:definition "An StL (‘StereoLithography’) file is a triangular representation of a 3-dimensional surface geometry. The surface is tessellated or broken down logically into a series of small triangles (facets). Each facet is described by a perpendicular direction and three points representing the vertices (corners) of the triangle. These data are used by a slicing algorithm to determine the cross sections of the 3-dimensional shape to be built by the fabber. The StL standard includes two data formats, ASCII and binary."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/STL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "StL"@en, "StL"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/svg> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Scalable Vector Graphics"@en; skos:definition "Open standard for two-dimensional vector graphics."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SVG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SVG"@en, "SVG"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/swm> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Split WIM file"@en; skos:definition "Split WIM file is a Windows Imaging Format file that has been split into multiple parts."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/SWM>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "SWM"@en, "SWM"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tab> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "MapInfo TAB is the media type which shall be used for the MapInfo TAB format. The file is a zip archive that contains at least the tab, dat, map and id files."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TAB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MapInfo TAB file"@en, "MapInfo TAB fail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tab_rstr> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "MapInfo TAB raster file is the media type which shall be used for the MapInfo Raster TAB format. This media type is incomplete as it lacks a reference to the specification of the format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TAB_RSTR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "MapInfo TAB raster file"@en, "MapInfo TAB rasterfail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tar> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Tape Archive"@en; skos:definition "TAR – tape archive – is a computer software utility for collecting many files into one archive file for distribution or backup purposes."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TAR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TAR"@en, "TAR"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tar_gz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Compressed Tarball File"@en; skos:definition "TAR – tape archive – is a computer software utility for collecting many files into one archive file, often referred to as a tarball, for distribution or backup purposes. GZ – gzip – is a file format and a software application used for file compression and decompression."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TAR_GZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TAR GZ"@en, "TAR GZ"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tar_xz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "XZ Compressed Tar Archive"@en; skos:definition "TAR – tape archive – is a computer software utility for collecting many files into one archive file, often referred to as a tarball, for distribution or backup purposes. XZ is a lossless compression program and file format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TAR_XZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TAR XZ"@en, "TAR XZ"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/thrift_binary> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apache Thrift binary format"@en; skos:definition "interface definition language and binary communication protocol used for defining and creating services for programming languages; binary format"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/THRIFT_BINARY>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Thrift binary"@en, "Thrift binary"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/thrift_compact> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apache Thrift compact binary format"@en; skos:definition "interface definition language and binary communication protocol used for defining and creating services for programming languages; more compact binary format"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/THRIFT_COMPACT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Thrift compact"@en, "Thrift compact"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/thrift_json> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Apache Thrift JSON format"@en; skos:definition "interface definition language and binary communication protocol used for defining and creating services for programming languages; JSON format"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/THRIFT_JSON>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Thrift JSON"@en, "Thrift JSON"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tiff> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Tagged Image Format File"@en; skos:definition "TIFF – Tagged Image File Format – is a computer file format for storing raster graphics images, popular among graphic artists, the publishing industry and photographers. TIFF is widely supported by scanning, faxing, word processing, optical character recognition, image manipulation, desktop publishing and page-layout applications. The format was created by Aldus Corporation for use in desktop publishing."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TIFF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TIFF"@en, "TIFF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tiff_fx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Tagged Image Format File Fax eXtended"@en; skos:definition "TIFF-FX is a TIFF-based file format created for fax sendings over the Internet."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TIFF_FX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TIFF FX"@en, "TIFF FX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tmx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Translation Memory eXchange"@en; skos:definition "TMX – Translation Memory eXchange – is an XML specification for the exchange of translation memory data between computer-aided translation and localization tools with little or no loss of critical data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TMX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TMX"@en, "TMX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/tsv> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Tab-Separated Value"@en; skos:definition "TSV – tab-separated values – files are a simple text format for storing data in a tabular structure, e.g. database table or spreadsheet data, and a way of exchanging information between databases. Each record in the table is one line of the text file. Each field value of a record is separated from the next by a tab character."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TSV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "TSV"@en, "TSV"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/txt> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Text file"@en; skos:definition "Plain text is the data (e.g. file contents) that represent only characters of readable material but not its graphical representation nor other objects. It may also include a limited number of characters that control simple arrangement of text, such as line breaks or tabulation characters. Plain text is different from formatted text, where style information is included, and from ‘binary files’ in which some portions must be interpreted as binary objects (encoded integers, real numbers, images, etc.)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TXT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Plain text"@en, "Plain text"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/ungen> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "ArcGIS ungenerate"@en; skos:definition "ArcGIS ungenerate creates a text file of x,y coordinates from the input coverage. It provides a useful mechanism to create simple coordinate files from coverages. This allows you to easily transfer coverages to other mapping systems or view and update individual coordinates using your computer’s text editor."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/UNGEN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Ungen"@en, "Ungen"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/vcf> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Variant Call Format"@en; skos:definition "standard text file format used in bioinformatics for storing gene sequence or DNA sequence variations"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/VCF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "VCF"@en, "VCF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/war> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Archive"@en; skos:definition "A WAR file is used to distribute a collection of JAR-files, JavaServer Pages, Java Servlets, Java classes, XML files, tag libraries, static web pages and other resources that together constitute a web application."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WAR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WAR"@en, "WAR"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/warc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Archive format"@en; skos:definition "WARC is a web archive format which specifies a method for combining multiple digital resources into an aggregate archive file together with related information."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WARC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WARC"@en, "WARC"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/warc_gz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Compressed Web Archive format"@en; skos:definition "WARC is a web archive format which specifies a method for combining multiple digital resources into an aggregate archive file together with related information. WARC GZ is WARC compressed by GZIP."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WARC_GZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WARC GZ"@en, "WARC GZ"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/wav> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Waveform Audio File"@en; skos:definition "Waveform Audio File (WAV) is a format is used for storing uncompressed digital audio files. It is the default audio format for Windows but it is supported by most operating systems."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WAV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WAV"@en, "WAV"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/wcs_srvc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Coverage Service"@en; skos:definition "The Open Geospatial Consortium Web Coverage Service Interface Standard (WCS) defines Web-based retrieval of coverages – that is, digital geospatial information representing space/time-varying phenomena."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WCS_SRVC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WCS"@en, "WCS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/webp> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "WebP image"@en; skos:definition "WebP is an image file format developed by Google intended as a replacement for JPEG, PNG, and GIF file formats. It supports both lossy and lossless compression, as well as animation and alpha transparency."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WEBP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WebP"@en, "WebP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/wfs_srvc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Feature Service"@en; skos:definition "The Open Geospatial Consortium Web Feature Service (WFS) Interface Standard provides an interface allowing requests for geospatial features across the web using platform-independent mechanisms and is independent of the underlying data store."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WFS_SRVC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WFS"@en, "WFS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/wim> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Windows Imaging Format"@en; skos:definition "The Windows Imaging Format (WIM) is a file-based disk image format."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WIM>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WIM"@en, "WIM"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/wms_srvc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Map Service"@en; skos:definition "A Web Map Service (WMS) is a standard protocol developed by the Open Geospatial Consortium (OGC) for serving georeferenced map images over the Internet. These images are typically produced by a map server from data provided by a geographic information system (GIS) database."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WMS_SRVC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WMS"@en, "WMS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/wmts_srvc> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Web Map Tile Service"@en; skos:definition "Open Geospatial Consortium’s standard for serving digital maps using predefined image tiles"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WMTS_SRVC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "WMTS"@en, "WMTS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/world> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "A world file is a plain text computer data file used by geographic information systems (GIS) to georeference raster map images. The file extension usually depends on the format of the associated image, e.g. .jgw for JPEG (2000) or .tfw for TIFF."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/WORLD>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "World file"@en, "World file"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xhtml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Extensible Hypertext Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "XHTML is a family of current and future document types and modules that reproduce, subset and extend HTML 4. XHTML family document types are XML based."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XHTML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XHTML"@en, "XHTML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xhtml5> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Extensible Hypertext Markup Language 5"@en; skos:definition "XML documents must be served with an XML Internet media type (often called ‘MIME type’) such as application/xhtml+xml or application/xml, and must conform to strict, well-formed syntax of XML. XHTML 5 is simply XML-serialized HTML 5 data (that is, HTML 5 constrained to XHTML’s strict requirements, e.g., not having any unclosed tags), sent with one of XML media types. HTML that has been written to conform to both the HTML and XHTML specifications and therefore produces the same DOM tree whether parsed as HTML or XML is known as polyglot markup. There is no DTD for XHTML5."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XHTML5>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XHTML5"@en, "XHTML5"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xhtml_simpl> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Extensible Hypertext Markup Language, simplified"@en; skos:definition "XHTML is HTML written as XML. Its simplified version is used for storage in the Publications Office."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XHTML_SIMPL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XHTML simplified"@en, "XHTML lihtsustatud"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xliff> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "XML Localisation Interchange File Format"@en; skos:definition "XLIFF is the XML Localisation Interchange File Format designed by a group of multilingual content publishers, software providers, localization service providers, localization tools providers and researchers. It is intended to give any multilingual content owner a single interchange file format that can be understood by any localization provider, using any conformant localization tool. While the primary focus is on being a lossless interchange format, usage of XLIFF as a processing format is neither encouraged nor discouraged or prohibited."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XLIFF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XLIFF"@en, "XLIFF"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xls> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Microsof Excel Workbook"@en; skos:definition "XLS is a proprietary binary file format used for Microsoft Excel spreadsheet which features calculation, graphing tools, pivot tables and a macro programming language."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XLS>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Excel XLS"@en, "Excel XLS"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xlsb> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Excel Binary Workbook"@en; skos:definition "A file with the XLSB file extension is an Excel Binary Workbook file. They store information in binary format instead of XML like with most other Excel files (like XLSX). Since XLSB files are binary, they can be read from and written to much faster, making them extremely useful for very large spreadsheets."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XLSB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XLSB"@en, "XLSB"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xlsm> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Excel Macro-enabled Workbook"@en; skos:definition "An Excel Macro-enabled Workbook contains worksheets of cells arranged by rows and columns as well as embedded macros programmed in the Visual Basic for Applications (VBA) language. XLSM files are saved in the Open XML format introduced in Microsoft Office 2007. XLSM files are XLSX files, but with macros enabled."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XLSM>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XLSM"@en, "XLSM"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xlsx> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Office Open XML Workbook"@en; skos:definition "XLSX is the default file format for Excel 2007 and later workbook used for Microsoft Excel spreadsheet which features calculation, graphing tools, pivot tables and a macro programming language. XLSX is in reality a ZIP compressed archive with a directory structure of XML text documents."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XLSX>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Excel XLSX"@en, "Excel XLSX"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Extensible Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "XML – Extensible Markup Language – is a markup language that defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable. The design goals of XML emphasize simplicity, generality and usability across the Internet."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XML"@en, "XML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xslfo> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Extensible Stylesheet Language – Formatting Objects"@en; skos:definition "XSL-FO – XSL Formatting Objects – is a markup language for XML document formatting that is most often used to generate PDF files. XSL-FO is part of XSL (Extensible Stylesheet Language), a set of W3C technologies designed for the transformation and formatting of XML data."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XSLFO>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XSL-FO"@en, "XSL-FO"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xslt> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Extensible Stylesheet Language Transformations"@en; skos:definition "XSLT – Extensible Stylesheet Language Transformations – is a language for transforming XML documents into other XML documents or other formats such as HTML for web pages, plain text or XSL Formatting Objects, which may subsequently be converted to other formats, such as PDF, PostScript and PNG."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XSLT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XSLT"@en, "XSLT"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xyz> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "The XYZ file format is a chemical file format. There is no formal standard and several variations exist, but a typical XYZ format specifies the molecule geometry by giving the number of atoms with Cartesian coordinates that will be read on the first line, a comment on the second, and the lines of atomic coordinates in the following lines."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XYZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "XYZ Chemical File"@en, "XYZ keemiline fail"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/xz> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "xz compressed file"@en; skos:definition "Compressed file produced using XZ Utils (free software command-line lossless data compressors, including LZMA and xz)."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XZ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "xz"@en, "xz"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/yaml> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "YAML Ain't Markup Language"@en; skos:definition "YAML is a human-friendly, cross language, Unicode based data serialization language designed around the common native data types of dynamic programming languages. It is broadly useful for programming needs ranging from configuration files to internet messaging to object persistence to data auditing and visualization."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/YAML>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "YAML"@en, "YAML"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/z> a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Unix compressed file"@en; skos:definition "Compressed file produced by Unix shell compression program based on the LZW (Lempel-Ziv-Welch) compression algorithm."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/Z>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "Z"@en, "Z"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes/zip> a skos:Concept; skos:definition "ZIP is an archive file format that supports lossless data compression. A ZIP file may contain one or more files or directories that may have been compressed."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/ZIP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/filetypes>; skos:prefLabel "ZIP"@en, "ZIP"@et .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/0d0> ccmm_props:XML_LNG "ca-valencia"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "valencià"@ca; skos:definition "Valencian is a Catalan dialect spoken in the Valencian Community in Spain.The Valencian Academy of the Language considers Catalan and Valencian to be simply two names for the same language."@en, "Le valencien est un dialecte catalan parlé dans la Communauté de Valence en Espagne.L’Académie valencienne de la langue considère simplement le catalan et le valencien comme deux noms pour la même langue."@fr; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/0D0>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "валенсиански"@bg, "valencijština"@cs, "valenciansk"@da, "Valencianisch"@de, "βαλενθιανά"@el, "Valencian"@en, "valenciano"@es, "valencia keel"@et, "valencia"@fi, "valencien"@fr, "Vaileinsis"@ga, "valencijski"@hr, "valenciai"@hu, "valenziano"@it, "valensiečių kalba"@lt, "valensiešu valoda"@lv, "Valenzjan"@mt, "Valenciaans"@nl, "valensiansk"@no, "walencki"@pl, "valenciano"@pt, "valenciană"@ro, "валенсийский язык"@ru, "valencijčina"@sk, "valencijanščina"@sl, "valencianska"@sv, "valensiyaca"@tr, "валенсійська мова"@uk .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/0e0> ccmm_props:XML_LNG "sr-ME"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "crnogorski jezik"@crn, "црногорски језик"@crn; skos:definition "Montenegrin is the standardised variety of the Serbo-Croatian used by Montenegrins. It is based on the Shtokavian dialect of Serbo-Croatian.Montenegrin uses more the Latin alphabet than the Cyrillic. In both alphabets there are two additional letters."@en, "Le monténégrin est la variante normalisée du serbo-croate utilisé par les Monténégrins. Il est basé sur le dialecte chtokavien du serbo-croate.Le monténégrin emploie plus l’alphabet latin que cyrillique. Dans les deux alphabets, il y a deux lettres supplémentaires."@fr; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/0E0>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "чарнагорская мова"@be, "черногорски"@bg, "crnogorski jezik"@bs, "montenegrí"@ca, "černohorština"@cs, "montenegrinsk"@da, "Montenegrinisch"@de, "μαυροβουνιακά"@el, "Montenegrin"@en, "montenegrino"@es, "montenegro keel"@et, "montenegro"@fi, "monténégrin"@fr, "Montainéigris"@ga, "crnogorski"@hr, "montenegrói"@hu, "svartfellska"@is, "montenegrino"@it, "juodkalniečių kalba"@lt, "melnkalniešu valoda"@lv, "црногорски јазик"@mk, "Montenegrin"@mt, "Montenegrijns"@nl, "montenegrinsk"@no, "czarnogórski"@pl, "montenegrino"@pt, "muntenegreană"@ro, "черногорский язык"@ru, "crnogorski"@sh, "čiernohorčina"@sk, "črnogorščina"@sl, "malazishtja"@sq, "црногорски језик"@sr, "montenegrinska"@sv, "karadağca"@tr, "чорногорська мова"@uk .
