<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/adb> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "adb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "adb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Atauran"@adb; skos:definition "Atauran is an Austronesian language spoken on Atauro island and in Manatuto Municipality, East Timor. It belongs to the Malayo-Polynesian sub-branch of Austronesian languages and is closely related to Wetarese and Galoli. The three main dialects of Atauran are Rasua, Raklungu and Hresuk."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ADB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Atauran"@en .
