<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/bap> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "bap"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "bap"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Bantawa"@bap; skos:definition "Bantawa is a Kiranti language spoken in the eastern Himalayan hills of eastern Nepal by Kirati Bantawa ethnic groups. The Kiranti languages form a branch of the Sino-Tibetan languages, one of the largest language families in the world. Kirati Bantawa groups use a syllabic alphabet system known as Kirat Rai."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/BAP>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Bantawa"@en .
