<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/bvr> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "bvr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "bvr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Burarra"@bvr; skos:definition "Burarra is a stable Australian Aboriginal language spoken in Arnhem Land. It is closely related to Gurr-goni, and both belong to the Maningrida group of languages. This group is sometimes classified with the Gunwinyguan languages in a proposed Macro-Gunwinyguan family, which is distinct from the Pama–Nyungan language family."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/BVR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Burarra"@en .
