<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/cwd> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "cwd"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "cwd"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Nīhithawīwin"@cwd, "Īthiniwīwin"@cwd; skos:definition "Woods Cree is a variety of the Cree macrolanguage. It is spoken in Northern Manitoba, Northern Saskatchewan and Northern Alberta, Canada. It is part of the Cree-Montagnais-Naskapi dialect continuum. Like other Cree-Montagnais-Naskapi varieties, Woods Cree is classified under the Algonquian branch of the Algic language family."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/CWD>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Woods Cree"@en .
