<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/deu> ccmm_props:ISO_639_1 "de"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_1>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2B "ger"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2B>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2T "deu"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2T>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "deu"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "de"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "German is a West Germanic language, most closely related to Dutch and Yiddish. German is a pluricentric language, with multiple countries having their own standardised variants as well as many dialects. There is also one variant referred to as Standard German."@en, "L’allemand est une langue germanique occidentale, proche du néerlandais et du yiddish. L’allemand est une langue pluricentrique, avec plusieurs pays ayant leurs propres variantes normalisées ainsi que de nombreux dialectes. Il existe aussi une variante dénommée «allemand standard»."@fr; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/DEU>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "немски"@bg, "němčina"@cs, "tysk"@da, "Deutsch"@de, "γερμανικά"@el, "German"@en, "alemán"@es, "saksa keel"@et, "saksa"@fi, "allemand"@fr, "Gearmáinis"@ga, "njemački"@hr, "němska"@hsb, "német"@hu, "þýska"@is, "tedesco"@it, "vokiečių kalba"@lt, "vācu valoda"@lv, "германски"@mk, "Ġermaniż"@mt, "Duits"@nl, "tysk"@no, "niemiecki"@pl, "alemão"@pt, "germană"@ro, "немецкий"@ru, "nemački"@sh, "nemčina"@sk, "nemščina"@sl, "немачки"@sr, "tyska"@sv, "almanca"@tr, "німецька мова"@uk .
