<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/dgr> ccmm_props:ISO_639_2B "dgr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2B>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2T "dgr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2T>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "dgr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "dgr"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Tłı̨chǫ"@dgr, "Dogrib"@en; skos:definition "Tlicho, also known as Tłı̨chǫ Yatıì or the Dogrib language, is a Northern Athabaskan language spoken by the Tłı̨chǫ (Dogrib people) First Nations of the Canadian Northwest Territories. It is part of the Na-Dené language family and the disputed Dené–Yeniseian hypothesis."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/DGR>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Tlicho"@en .
