<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/env> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "env"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "env"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Enwan"@env; skos:definition "Enwan (Edo State) is an Edoid language spoken in Edo State in Nigeria. With Ikpeshi and Ivbie North-Okpela-Arhe, it forms the Ikpeshic subgroup. Similar to the more well-known Bantu languages, Edoid languages also feature noun class systems, which are a key characteristic used to identify the broader Atlantic–Congo language family, to which Enwan belongs as part of the Volta–Congo primary branch."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENV>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Enwan (Edu State)"@en .
