<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/gge> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "gge"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "gge"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Guragone"@en, "Gurr-goni"@gge; skos:definition "Gurr-goni, or Guragone, is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language spoken in Arnhem Land. In 2011 it had about 60 speakers, all of whom were also fluent in Burarra or Kuninjku. It is closely related to Burarra, and both belong to the Maningrida group of languages. This group is sometimes classified with the Gunwinyguan languages in a proposed Macro-Gunwinyguan family, which is distinct from the Pama–Nyungan language family."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/GGE>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Gurr-goni"@en .
