<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/gni> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "gni"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "gni"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Gooniyandi"@gni; skos:definition "Gooniyandi, or Guniyandi, is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language spoken by about 200 people, most of whom live in or near Fitzroy Crossing in Kimberley, Western Australia. Gooniyandi is not related to the Pama-Nyungan language family that spans the majority of Australia; however, it is a relative of Bunuba. Both belong to the Bunuban language family."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/GNI>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Gooniyandi"@en .
