<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/hng> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "hng"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "hng"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Dihungu"@hng, "Kihungu"@hng; skos:definition "Hungu is a Southern Bantoid language spoken in Angola. It is considered an endangered language. Hungu belongs to the Kikongo group, which is classified within the Volta-Congo branch. Like other Bantu and Bantoid languages, hungu has a noun class system, a characteristic feature of languages belonging to the Atlantic–Congo lineage, the largest demonstrated language family in Africa."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/HNG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Hungu"@en .
