<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/ihw> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "ihw"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "ihw"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Bidawal"@en, "mŭk-dhang"@ihw; skos:definition "Bidhawal was an Australian Aboriginal language, either a dialect of or closely related to the Kurnai language. The Bidawal called their own dialect mŭk-dhang (‘good speech’), and that of the neighbouring Kurnai gūnggala-dhang 'strangers' language'. Both languages are classified within the Ganaic branch of the Pama-Nyungan languages, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/IHW>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Bidhawal"@en .
