<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/iin> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "iin"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "iin"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Thiin"@iin; skos:definition "Thiin is a nearly extinct Mantharta language of the Pilbara region in Western Australia. It is closely related to Djiwarli (dze). Together with other Mantharta languages it belongs to the Pama–Nyungan language family, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/IIN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Thiin"@en .
