<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/jay> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "jay"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "jay"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Nhangu"@en, "Yan-nhangu"@jay; skos:definition "Yan-nhangu, also known as Nhangu, is a Pama-Nyungan language within the Yolngu sub-branch. It is spoken by the Yan-nhangu people in Australia's Northern Territory. The Pama–Nyungan languages are the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/JAY>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Yan-nhangu"@en .
