<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/kmb> ccmm_props:ISO_639_2B "kmb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2B>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2T "kmb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2T>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "kmb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "kmb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Kimbundu"@kmb; skos:definition "Kimbundu is a narrow Bantu language spoken in the north-west of Angola. It is the second-most-widely-spoken Bantu language in Angola. Together with Mpinda (pnd) and Kibala (blv), it belongs to the Mbundu group, which is classified within the Volta-Congo primary branch. Like other Bantu languages, Mpinda has a noun class system, a characteristic feature of languages belonging to the Atlantic–Congo lineage, the largest demonstrated language family in Africa."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/KMB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Kimbundu"@en .
