<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/lit> ccmm_props:ISO_639_1 "lt"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_1>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2B "lit"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2B>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2T "lit"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2T>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "lit"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "lt"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:definition "Lithuanian is one of the two living members of the Baltic languages, the other being Latvian. It is the official language of Lithuania.The Lithuanian language is often said to be the most conservative living Indo-European language, retaining many features of Proto-Indo-European now lost in other Indo-European languages."@en, "Le lituanien est l’un des deux membres vivants des langues baltes, l’autre étant le letton. C’est la langue officielle de la Lituanie.Le lituanien est souvent dit la langue indo-européenne vivante la plus conservatrice, gardant de nombreuses caractéristiques de l’indo-européen aujourd’hui perdues dans d’autres langues indo-européennes."@fr; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/LIT>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "литовски"@bg, "litevština"@cs, "litauisk"@da, "Litauisch"@de, "λιθουανικά"@el, "Lithuanian"@en, "lituano"@es, "leedu keel"@et, "liettua"@fi, "lituanien"@fr, "Liotuáinis"@ga, "litavski"@hr, "litawšćina"@hsb, "litván"@hu, "litháíska"@is, "lituano"@it, "lietuvių kalba"@lt, "lietuviešu valoda"@lv, "литвански"@mk, "Litwan"@mt, "Litouws"@nl, "litauisk"@no, "litewski"@pl, "lituano"@pt, "lituaniană"@ro, "литовский"@ru, "litvanski"@sh, "litovčina"@sk, "litovščina"@sl, "литвански"@sr, "litauiska"@sv, "litvanca"@tr, "литовська мова"@uk .
