<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/ltc> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "ltc"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "ltc"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Middle Chinese"@en, "Zhōnggǔ Hànyǔ"@ltc, "中古汉语"@ltc; skos:definition "Middle Chinese (formerly known as Ancient Chinese) or the Qieyun system (QYS) is the historical variety of Chinese recorded in the Qieyun, a rime dictionary first published in 601 and followed by several revised and expanded editions. Most scholars now believe that it records a compromise between northern and southern reading and poetic traditions from the late Northern and Southern dynasties period. This composite system contains important information for the reconstruction of the preceding system of Old Chinese phonology. Linguists sometimes refer to the system of the Qieyun as Early Middle Chinese and the variant revealed by the rime tables as Late Middle Chinese."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/LTC>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "късен среднокитайски"@bg, "pozdní střední čínština"@cs, "sen middelkinesisk"@da, "spätes Mittelchinesisch"@de, "Ύστερα μέσα κινεζικά"@el, "Late Middle Chinese"@en, "chino medio tardío"@es, "hiliskeskhiina"@et, "myöhäiskeskikiina"@fi, "chinois moyen tardif"@fr, "Meán-Sínis Dhéanach"@ga, "kasni srednjekineski"@hr, "késői középkínai"@hu, "tardo cinese medio"@it, "vėlyvoji vidurinė kinų"@lt, "vēlā vidusķīniešu valoda"@lv, "Ċiniż Nofsani Tardiv"@mt, "Laatmiddelchinees"@nl, "późny średniochiński"@pl, "chinês medieval tardio"@pt, "chineză mijlocie târzie"@ro, "neskorá stredná čínština"@sk, "pozna srednja kitajščina"@sl, "sen medeltidskinesiska"@sv .
