<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/mnk> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "mnk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "mnk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "mandinka"@cs, "jezik naroda Mandinka"@hr, "Mandinka"@mnk, "لغة مندنكا"@mnk, "jezik mandinka"@sl; skos:definition "Mandinka (Mandingo) is a Mande language spoken by the Mandinka people in Senegal, the Gambia and Guinea-Bissau. Mandinka is written by Latin or Arabic scripts. Mande languages are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/MNK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "мандинка"@bg, "mandingština"@cs, "mandinka"@da, "Mandinka"@de, "μαντίνκα"@el, "Mandinka"@en, "Mandinká"@es, "mandinka keel"@et, "mandinka"@fi, "mandinka"@fr, "Mandancais"@ga, "mandinka"@hr, "mandinka"@hu, "Mandinka"@it, "mandinkų kalba"@lt, "mandinka valoda"@lv, "Mandinka"@mt, "Mandinka"@nl, "mandinka"@pl, "mandinga"@pt, "mandinka"@ro, "мандинка"@ru, "mandinka"@sk, "mandinščina"@sl, "mandinka"@sv, "мандінка"@uk .
