<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/nay> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "nay"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "nay"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Ngarrindjeri"@nay; skos:definition "Ngarrindjeri is a dormant Aboriginal language spoken in South Australia. It belongs to the Pama–Nyungan languages, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of Australia’s roughly 400 Aboriginal languages. There were 312 speakers of Ngarrindjerri recorded in the 2016 Australian census. Language maintenance and revival has increased during the early 21st century."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/NAY>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Ngarrindjeri"@en .
