<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/nbj> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "nbj"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "nbj"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Ngarinyman"@nbj; skos:definition "Ngarinyman is an endangered Pama–Nyungan language spoken by the Ngarinyman in the Northern Territory, Australia. It is closely related to Gurindji, and sometimes considered a dialect of Gurindji. Both belong to the Ngumpin sub-group within the Pama-Nyungan language family, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/NBJ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Ngarinyman"@en .
