<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/nig> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "nig"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "nig"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Ngalakgan"@nig; skos:definition "Ngalakgan is an extinct Australian Aboriginal language of the Ngalakgan people. It has not been fully acquired by children since the 1930s. It is one of the Northern Non-Pama–Nyungan languages formerly spoken in the Roper river region of the Northern Territory. It is closely related to Rembarrnga (rmb). Both are classified within the Gunwinyguan language family."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/NIG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Ngalakgan"@en .
