<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/nyh> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "nyh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "nyh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Nyikina"@nyh; skos:definition "Nyikina is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language spoken by the Nyikina people in northern Western Australia. It is closely related to the extinct Warrwa language. Both belong to the small Nyulnyulan language family. Most languages in this family are extinct, with only three extant languages, all of which are almost extinct"@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/NYH>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Nyikina"@en .
