<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/pzn> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "pzn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "pzn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Para Naga"@en, "Jejara"@pzn; skos:definition "Jejara Naga is a Tibeto-Burman language classified under the Kuki-Chin–Naga sub-branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family. The Jejara Naga, also known as the Para Naga, are one of the major Naga peoples of Myanmar and primarily inhabit the area around Lay Shi Township."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/PZN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Jejara Naga"@en .
