<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/rif> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "rif"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "rif"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Tarifit"@rif; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/RIF>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "tarifit"@rif .
<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/ril> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "ril"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "ril"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Yinnet"@en, "Riang Lang"@ril; skos:definition "Riang Lang is a Palaungic language of Myanmar. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic language family. Speakers are culturally assimilated with the Karen, but are Palaung by ancestry and their language is unrelated. Riang Lang (Yinnet) and Riang Lai (Yinchia) are sometimes considered distinct languages, sometimes the same language. Like many Austroasiatic languages, Palaungic languages are characterised by prefixation in its clause structure and larger than average vowel inventories."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/RIL>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Riang Lang"@en .
