<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/sne> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "sne"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "sne"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Jagoi"@en, "Bau Bidayuh"@sne; skos:definition "Bau Bidayuh is a Dayak language of Borneo. It is closely related to the Bukar-Sadung Bidayuh (sdo), Biatah Bidayuh (bth) and Tringgus-Sembaan Bidayuh (trx) languages. Bau Bidayuh belongs to the Malayo-Polyneasian primary branch of the Austronesian language family. Two main morphological characteristics of the Malayo-Polynesian languages are a system of affixation and reduplication to form new words."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/SNE>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Bau Bidayuh"@en .
