<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/tbh> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "tbh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "tbh"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Thurawal"@en, "Dharawal"@tbh; skos:definition "Dharawal, also known as Thurawal, is a dormant Pama-Nyungan language classified within the Yuin-Kuri sub-branch. It was spoken in Wollongong, Port Kembla, and Nowra regions of New South Wales, Australia. The Pama–Nyungan languages are the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/TBH>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Dharawal"@en .
