<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/tuk> ccmm_props:ISO_639_1 "tk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_1>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2B "tuk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2B>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_2T "tuk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_2T>; ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "tuk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "tk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "türkmen dili"@tk, "түркмен дили"@tk; skos:definition "Turkmen or Turkoman is spoken in Asia. Turkmen is a member of the East Oghuz branch of the Turkic family of languages; its closest relatives being Anatolian Turkish and Azerbaijani, with which it shares a relatively high degree of mutual intelligibility.Officially, Turkmen currently is rendered in the ‘Täze Elipbiý’, or ‘New Alphabet’, which is based on the Latin alphabet. However, the old ‘Soviet’ Cyrillic alphabet is still in wide use."@en, "Le turkmène est une langue appartenant au groupe des langues turques, parlée en Asie centrale, principalement au Turkménistan.Le turkmène a été écrit avec un alphabet arabe adapté, puis un alphabet latin jusqu’en 1940. L’État soviétique force alors l’adoption d’une variante de l’alphabet cyrillique pour l’écriture du turkmène. Depuis 1997, l’alphabet officiel est une variante de l’alphabet latin avec quelques diacritiques, proche de celui du turc."@fr; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/TUK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "туркменски"@bg, "turkmenština"@cs, "turkmensk"@da, "Turkmenisch"@de, "τουρκμενικά"@el, "Turkmen"@en, "turcomano"@es, "türkmeeni keel"@et, "turkmeeni"@fi, "turkmène"@fr, "Tuircméinis"@ga, "turkmenski"@hr, "turkmenšćina"@hsb, "türkmén"@hu, "túrkmenska"@is, "turkmeno"@it, "turkmėnų kalba"@lt, "turkmēņu valoda"@lv, "туркменски"@mk, "Turkmen"@mt, "Turkmeens"@nl, "turkmensk"@no, "turkmeński"@pl, "turquemeno"@pt, "turkmenă"@ro, "туркменский"@ru, "turkmenski"@sh, "turkménčina"@sk, "turkmenščina"@sl, "туркменски"@sr, "turkmeniska"@sv, "türkmence"@tr, "туркменська мова"@uk .
