<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/unn> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "unn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "unn"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Gunaikurnai"@en, "mŭk-dhang"@unn; skos:definition "Kurnai is an Australian Aboriginal language spoken in Gippsland in south-east Victoria. Bidawal (ihw) was either a divergent dialect or a closely related language. The Kurnai called their own dialect mŭk-dhang, and that of the Bidawal kwai-thang (‘rough speech’). Both languages are classified within the Ganaic branch of the Pama-Nyungan languages, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/UNN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Kurnai"@en .
