<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/uth> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "uth"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "uth"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Eastern Duka"@en, "Saare"@uth, "it-Hun"@uth; skos:definition "ut-Hun, also known as Eastern Duka, is a Northwestern Kainji language of Nigeria. It is close to us-Saare, also known as Western Duka. However, speakers use Saare for both languages. Noun class systems are a defining feature of the Atlantic–Congo languages, to which Kainji languages belong as part of the Volta-Congo primary branch and the Benue-Congo sub-branch."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/UTH>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "ut-Hun"@en .
