<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/vjk> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "vjk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "vjk"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Vajjika"@en, "बज्जिका"@vjk; skos:definition "Bajjika is an Indo-Aryan language variety, which in turn belongs to the Indo-European language family. It is spoken in the north-western part of Bihar, India and in Nepal. It is also classified as a dialect of Maithili language and is known as Western Maithili. In the 1960s and the 1970s, when the Maithili speakers demanded a separate Mithila state, the Angika and Bajjika speakers made counter-demands for recognition of their languages."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/VJK>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Bajjika"@en .
