<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/waq> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "waq"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "waq"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Wagiman"@waq; skos:definition "Wagiman is a near-extinct Aboriginal Australian language spoken by only two elderly people (2021), who live in and around Pine Creek, in the Katherine Region of the Northern Territory. The Wagiman language is notable for its complex system of verbal morphology, which remains under-investigated, its possession of a cross-linguistically rare part of speech called a coverb, its complex predicates and for its ability to derive verbs from coverb roots, which is a unique feature among Australian languages. Wagiman is a language isolate, but may still bear a remote relation with its neighbouring languages but this is yet to be demonstrated."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WAQ>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Wagiman"@en .
