<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/wgg> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "wgg"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "wgg"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Wangganguru"@en, "Wangkangurru"@wgg; skos:definition "Wangkangurru is a moribund Pama-Nyungan language spoken in Simpson Desert area in the state of South Australia. It classified within the Karnic sub-branch of the Pama–Nyungan languages, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WGG>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Wangkangurru"@en .
