<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/wyb> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "wyb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "wyb"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Ngiyambaa"@wyb, "Wangaaybuwan"@wyb, "Wayil"@wyb; skos:definition "Wangaaybuwan-Ngiyambaa is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language traditionally spoken by the Wangaaypuwan and Wayilwan peoples of New South Wales. Wangaaybuwan-Ngiyambaa is closely related to Wiradjuri (wrh). Together, they form the Wiradhuric sub-group within the Pama–Nyungan language family, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/WYB>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Wangaaybuwan-Ngiyambaa"@en .
