<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/yii> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "yii"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "yii"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Yidiny"@yii; skos:definition "Yidiny is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language spoken in the northeast of Queensland by the Yidinji people. It is closely related to Djabugay, and both are sometimes placed in a separate Yidinyic branch of the Pama–Nyungan language family, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/YII>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Yidiny"@en .
