<https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages/zin> ccmm_props:ISO_639_3 "zin"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3>; ccmm_props:XML_LNG "zin"^^<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG>; a skos:Concept; skos:altLabel "Dzinda"@en, "Zinza"@zin; skos:definition "Zinza is an East Bantu language spoken on the southern shore of Lake Victoria. It is classified within the Volta-Congo primary branch of the Atlantic-Congo language family. Like other Bantu languages, Zinza has a noun class system, a characteristic feature of languages belonging to the Atlantic–Congo lineage, the largest demonstrated language family in Africa."@en; skos:exactMatch <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ZIN>; skos:inScheme <https://nma.eosc.cz/vocabularies/languages>; skos:prefLabel "Zinza"@en .
